('Naan', NULL, NULL, '6 cups maida (white flour)
6 tsp. milk powder
200 grm. oil or margarine
1 cup evaporated milk
6 tsp. sugar
2 tsp. baking powder
1 egg
3 tsp. yeast', '1. Mix all the ingredients and knead into a dough.
2. Cover with a damp cloth and leave at room temperature for 2-3 hours.
3. Then divide it evenly into 12 parts.
4. Roll out into flat chapati which is as thick as a pizza crust.
5. Bake in oven at 350 F till light brown.
6. Can also be frozen after baking for later use.', 1328, 27.93, 183.16, 55.36, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Desi Cookbook — https://www.desicookbook.com/naan/'),
('Parhata', NULL, NULL, '2 cups Flour
1/4 tsp. Salt
1 cup water
Oil or ghee as need', '1. In flour add salt and mix.
2. Add a little water and mix.
3. The consistency should be soft and putty-like. It helps if you kneed it with a wet hand.
4. Keep the dough in the fridge for 5 minutes.
5. Divide this dough into 4 portions.
6. Roll each portion into a ball and flatten it into a chapati shape (round).
7. Spread a little oil or ghee on it.
8. Make a cut in it from the center to the edge.
9. Pick up the cut edge and start rolling it so that you end up with a cone.
10. With the palm of your hand flatten it while twisting it so that it once again forms a ball.
11. Flatten it again in chapati shape and fry it on medium to low heat with three tbsp oil or more depending on the size of the frying pan.
12. Turn it over once the bottom is golden brown.
13. When both sides are golden brown it’s done.', 234, 7.76, 47.67, 1.2, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Desi Cookbook — https://www.desicookbook.com/parhata/'),
('Meethi Imli Chutney', NULL, NULL, '250 gms. tamarind (Imli)
2 cups sugar
Salt according to taste
1/2 tsp chili (Lal Mirch) powder
½ inch piece of ginger (Adrak) or Dried ginger (Sounth)', '1. Soak the imli in lukewarm water for an hour or so until it softens.
2. Rub well to remove the seeds.
3. Strain out all the juice into a container.
4. Put on low heat and bring to boil.
5. Add sugar, salt and chili powder and keep stirring and cooking on low heat till it starts to become thick.
6. small piece of ginger can be added and later removed for an extra flavor.
7. When desired consistency achieved remove from heat and allow to cool before storing (in a jar with a lid).', 218, 0.79, 56.23, 0.2, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Desi Cookbook — https://www.desicookbook.com/meethi-imli-chutney/'),
('Khajur ki Chutney', NULL, NULL, '50 grm. pitted dates
15 grm. seedless raisins
1 tsp. cumin seeds (Zeera) powder
1 tsp chili (Lal Mirch) powder
1 heaped tsp. tamarind (Imli) concentrate OR 3 tbs. lemon juice
125 ml water
3/4 tsp salt
1 tsp brown sugar', '1. Put all the ingredients in a blender and mix well.
2. Strain and throw out the residue.
3. Serve the strained chutney with kababs, tikkas.', 35, 0.76, 8.77, 0.2, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Desi Cookbook — https://www.desicookbook.com/khajur-ki-chutney/'),
(NULL, NULL, NULL, '1 bundle of mint (Podina) leaves
1 tsp. salt
½ cup whole dried red chilies
5 tbs. tamarind (Imli) paste
2 green chilies', '1. Soak the Tamarind in water for an hour.
2. Remove the seeds from the tamarind.
3. Put everything into a grinder and grind until it''s a smooth paste.
4. Keep refrigerated', 19, 0.43, 4.62, 0.1, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Desi Cookbook — https://www.desicookbook.com/mint-chutney/'),
('Unday ka Halwa', NULL, NULL, '12 eggs
1 cup sugar
4-5 green cardamom (Chhoti ilaichi) - seeds
1 cup ghee (not oil)
dry fruits - pistachio (Pistay), almond (Badam), raisins (Kishmish)', '1. Mix all into a pot and cook over a low flame stirring
2. constantly till the mixture is light brown and dry.
3. Put onto a plate and flatten into a 1" layer.
4. After it cools down cut into small pieces.', 445, 9.58, 25.83, 34.38, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Desi Cookbook — https://www.desicookbook.com/unday-ka-halwa/'),
('Suji ka Halwa', NULL, NULL, '2 tbs. semolina (Suji)
2 tbs. oil
4 tbs. sugar
1/2 cup water
3 green cardamom (Chhoti Ilaichi)
yellow food color (optional)', '1. Put the suji and oil in a pot along with ilaichi seeds and fry until slightly brown on very low heat.
2. Meanwhile combine sugar and water to
3. make a syrup.
4. Add this to the suji taking care not to burn yourself and cook on low heat to desired consistency.
5. If you want to color the halwa add the color to the syrup before pouring it into the suji.', 129, 1.43, 17.27, 6.89, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Desi Cookbook — https://www.desicookbook.com/suji-ka-halwa/'),
('Shahi Tukray', NULL, NULL, '6 slices of bread
4-6 tbs sugar
dry fruit--Pistachio,almond
kevera essence
khoya or cream (Riccota cheese)
3-4 tbs oil
seeds of 4-5 green cardamom (Chhoti Ilaichi)
yellow food color
1 liter of milk', '1. Fry the slices of bread in a little oil until light brown. Remove and set it aside.
2. In milk add illaichi seeds,sugar,and color and cook until thick.
3. Arrange the bread slices in the milk and bring to boil.
4. Turn once to coat both sides.
5. Let milk thicken.
6. Then just before removing from heat add kevera
7. essence.
8. Garnish with cream and dry fruits', 404, 12.13, 43.27, 21.35, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Desi Cookbook — https://www.desicookbook.com/shahi-tukray/'),
('Sewaiyan', NULL, NULL, '100 grm. Sewayyan
4 tbs. ghee or butter
3-4 green cardamom (Chhoti Ilaichi)
4-5 tbs. sugar
1 cup water
1 pinch of yellow food color (optional)
2 tbs. Khoya or powdered milk (optional)
½ tsp. Kewra essence
Dry fruit (according to taste)', '1. In a pan add the ghee or butter and seeds of 3 cardamoms.
2. Add the Sewayyan and roast them on very low flame till their color changes to a darker shade.
3. Stir constantly. In another pan meanwhile add the sugar, water and seeds of 1 cardamom and also the yellow food color if you wish.
4. Bring to the boil and remove from heat.
5. When the Sewayyan have turned a browner shade add this sugar syrup to them all the while stirring constantly.
6. Add the khoya or powdered milk at this time if you like and the dry fruit.
7. Cover and let cook for 5-6 minutes till the water has dried and the sewayyian have become tender. Add the kewra essence and remove from heat.
8. Garnish with dry fruit and serve either plain or with fresh cream.
9. Can be served both hot and cold.', 205, 4.29, 24.23, 10.71, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Desi Cookbook — https://www.desicookbook.com/sewaiyan/'),
('Ras Malai', NULL, NULL, '1 cup powdered milk
1 egg
1 tsp. oil
1 tsp. baking powder
Syrup:
1 liter milk
6 tbs. sugar
1 green cardamom (Chhoti Ilaichi)
1 tbs. chopped pistachio (Pistay)
1/2 tsp. Kewra essence', '1. Mix together the ingredients into a dough and form into small oval, slightly flattened balls.
2. Meanwhile boil the milk with sugar and ilaichi seeds.
3. When the milk starts to boil add the malai balls.
4. When they start to swell up lower the heat and cook for 10 minutes.
5. Just before removing from heat add kewra essence.
6. Garnish with pista.
7. Chill and serve.', 155, 6.07, 17.77, 6.9, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Desi Cookbook — https://www.desicookbook.com/ras-malai/'),
('Ras Gullay', NULL, NULL, '1 liter of fresh milk
OR 2 cups of powdered milk dissolved in 12 cups of water.
2 cups sugar
1 tbs. vinegar or lemon juice
2 tbs. rice flour
2-3 drops of Kewra essence
chopped pistachio (Pistay) for garnish (optional)', '1. Heat the milk in a pot until it starts to boil and add vinegar/lemon juice to it to let it curdify. (My word). Keep boiling until the water and curd
2. separates out.
3. Drain and sieve it well to remove all the water from the curd. Spread the curd out on a clean, flat surface and add the rice flour to it.
4. Knead it as much as you can, the more the better
5. Meanwhile add the sugar to 3 cups of water and boil to make syrup.
6. When the syrup starts to boil make the curd into small round balls and add to the boiling syrup and cook for 10 - 15 minutes.
7. Just before removing from heat add the kewra essence and garnish with chopped pista.
8. Cool before serving', 562, 8.52, 115.55, 8.69, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Desi Cookbook — https://www.desicookbook.com/ras-gullay/'),
('Panjeeri', NULL, NULL, '6 tbs. flour or semolina
2 tbs. ghee
2 tbs. coconut (Narial)-gated
2 tbs. Pistachio (Pistay)-grated
2 tbs. Almond (Badam)-grated
100 grm. Makhanay
50 grm. Gond
1 tbs. Char Maghaz
½ tsp. dry dates (Chhuwaray)-chopped
2 tbs. dry fig (injeer)-chopped
2 tbs. cashew nuts (Kaju) crushed
¼ tsp. nutmeg (Jaiphal)
4 tbs. sugar
6 pcs. green cardamom (Chhoti Ilaichi)
½ tsp. dry ginger (Sounth)-grated', '1. Fry Ata/Suji, Makhanay, Gond in ghee till light brown.
2. Add all other ingredients mix well and fry for few minutes.', 173, 2.0, 17.13, 11.36, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Desi Cookbook — https://www.desicookbook.com/panjeeri/'),
('Naryal ka Meetha', NULL, NULL, '2 cups Coconut (fresh, grated) or
3 cups Coconut (desiccated)
4 cups Powdered Milk
1 can (175 ml) Evaporated Milk
½ cup Fresh milk, if required.
3 tbs Ghee
¾ cup Sugar
3 tbs Ghee (for greasing)
Pinch of Lemon Color', '1. Start with making khoya. Mix the powdered milk and ghee. Using evaporated milk, knead it into hard dough. Roll it to a hard ball and keep it in the freezer for 15-20 minutes.
2. Take out the khoya and grate it with a coarse grater.
3. In a pot heat the ghee, add coconut and fry a little.
4. Add khoya, color and sugar. Mix well and stir cook on low heat, use fresh milk if desired, till it has dried and it starts to come together leaving the sides of the pot.
5. Remove from heat and spread evenly in a greased flat dish to set.', 924, 7.93, 37.58, 87.76, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Desi Cookbook — https://www.desicookbook.com/naryal-ka-meetha/'),
('Kulfi', NULL, NULL, '1 cup or 160 ml evaporated full cream milk.
850 gms. Cream
2 slices of bread
500 gms. Condensed sweetened milk
½ cup water
6-8 green cardamom (Chhoti Ilaichi)-seeds crushed
10 pistachio-crushed
2 tbs. rose water
Few drops of Kewra', '1. Mix all the ingredients blend them well
2. Pour the mixture in popsicle containers and freeze', 1046, 19.72, 29.02, 98.19, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Desi Cookbook — https://www.desicookbook.com/kulfi/'),
('Khubani ka Meetha', NULL, NULL, '250 grm. Dried Apricot
2 cups water
3 tbs. sugar
½ liter milk
2 tbs. sugar for custard
2 tbs. custard powder
Fresh cream', '1. Presoak the apricot preferably overnight. Remove the pits and take out the almond from inside the pit and keep aside.
2. In a pot boil the apricot with 2 cups of water. Add the 3 TBS of sugar to this water. When the quantity of the water is reduced to 1-cup remove from heat. Cool and grind to a paste that is neither too thick nor too fine.
3. Add the almonds that were removed from the pits to this pulp mixture.
4. In another pot prepare the custard either according to instructions on the custard powder packet or according to the following.
5. Take ½ liter of milk. Bring to the boil. Add the 2 TBS of sugar. Meanwhile mix the 2 TBS of custard powder with a few TBS of milk and add to the boiling milk stirring constantly otherwise it will coagulate.
6. Cook for a few minutes till it thickens slightly. Remove from heat and cool.
7. Now in a dish you can do either one of the following
8. Add the custard then top off with a layer of the apricot pulp and then with a layer of fresh cream.
9. OR
10. Add a layer of custard then a layer of apricot one on top of the other. Then add a final layer of fresh cream.
11. Serve chilled.', 319, 9.57, 65.27, 5.12, 'Y', NULL, NULL, 'Desi Cookbook — https://www.desicookbook.com/khubani-ka-meetha/'),
('Jalebi', NULL, NULL, '1 cup maida
½ cup rice flour
2 cup water
2½ cup sugar
1 tsp. soda
¼ tsp. cream of tartar
6 green cardamom (Chhoti Ilaichi)
2 tsp. Rose water
Saffron (Zafran)
Yellow/orange food colour
Oil/ghee for frying', '1. Mix maida, rice flour, soda and water and keep the mixture overnight in warm place.
2. Mix sugar, water, ilaichi saffron cream of tartar and cook to make it into thick syrup.
3. Deep fry the mixture in the curls using a nozzle like the one used for icing of cakes. Fry till light brown and pour into the syrup. DO NOT OVER SOAK.
4. Remove and let the excess syrup drain out.', 472, 5.47, 113.77, 0.93, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Desi Cookbook — https://www.desicookbook.com/jalebi/'),
('Balushahi', NULL, NULL, '750 gms. Sugar
1 cup water to make syrup
500 gms. Maida
200 gms. Ghee for frying
1 tbs. yogurt
Orange food color
½ tsp. soda
1 tsp. baking powder
(if self raising flour is used soda and baking powder are not required)', '1. Mix sugar and water and cook to make syrup.
2. Mix other ingredients (except ghee) and water adequate to roll.
3. Make small patties and fry on low heat.
4. Soak in syrup briefly and let the syrup covering on the balushahi to dry.', 818, 6.69, 143.4, 25.55, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Desi Cookbook — https://www.desicookbook.com/balushahi/'),
('Classic Creamy Chocolate Mousse', NULL, NULL, '6 oz dark chocolate (55% or darker)
3 tbsp butter
3 egg yolks, lightly beaten
3 egg whites
1/2 tsp cream of tartar
1/4 cup sugar
1 cup whipping cream
2 tbsp sugar', '1. Melt the chocolate and butter together over a double boiler. Use a large bowl if possible or transfer to one once melted.
2. Let the mixture cool to room temp then briskly stir the egg yolks into the chocolate mix to avoid lumps. Set aside
3. Whip the egg whites till foamy then add the cream of tartar
4. Keep whipping until soft peaks form, i.e. a beater lifted out of whites will create a peak that folds over the top
5. Add the sugar in 1 tbsp at a time, mixing for a minute between additions to incorporate.
6. Keep beating until stiff peaks form, i.e. a beater lifted out of the meringue will result in a stiff peak of meringue
7. Beat the cream and sugar together till the cream is fluffy, a beater lifted out of the cream mix should see distinct peaks form
8. Fold about a quarter of the meringue into the egg yolk mixture to lighten it. When folding take care to gently swoop under and over to mix and not stir.
9. Now gradually fold in the remaining meringue in two more batches taking care to be gentle to help maintain texture.
10. Fold in the cream, refrigerate until ready to serve.', 494, 9.62, 29.84, 37.72, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/classic-creamy-chocolate-mousse/'),
('Herbed Chicken Burger w/ a DELISH herby sauce', NULL, 'Chicken Burger but with herbs so we call it "healthy"', '1 lb ground chicken
2/3 cup bread crumbs ((if your chicken is watery you made an additional 1/4 cup))
5 tbsp mayonnaise
1/4 cup chopped mint
1/4 cup chopped cilantro
6 scallions (white parts)
3/4 tsp salt
3/4 tsp soy sauce
1/2 tsp pepper
1/2 tsp ginger paste or grated ginger ((optional but adds great flavour!))
5 tbsp mayo
1/4 cup mint (finely chopped)
1/4 cup cilantro (finely chopped)
6 scallions - green parts, thinly sliced.
a squeeze of lime juice, salt and pepper.
6 Burger Buns
Sliced Onions, Tomatoes, Jalapenos for topping
Butter for your burger buns', '1. Tip: Before starting chop the scallions, separating the green and white parts, then chop the half cup of cilantro and mint too and set aside.
2. Combine all the chicken burger patty ingredients and form into 6 patties. Tip: for a less chunky textured burger (our preference) blend the mayo, jalapeno, mint, scallions and cilantro.
3. Cook in a pan for 4-5 minutes on each side on medium heat until done.
4. Add your minced herbs and scallions to the mayo and stir in lime juice.
5. Taste and adjust seasoning.
6. Toast your burger buns
7. Lightly butter the bottom bun, place the patty on top, add your favourite toppings (onions, jalapenos, tomatoes) and a generous spoonful of the sauce. Top with the top half of the bun and dig in.', 549, 29.11, 31.06, 34.06, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/herbed-chicken-burgers-with-a-delish-sauce/'),
('Coconut Macaroons w/ Unsweetened Coconut', NULL, 'Chewy delicious coconut macaroons made with condensed milk for an easy treat!', '2 Egg Whites
3 1/2 cup Unsweetened Shredded Coconut
300 ml Condensed Milk (1 can)
1/2 tsp Salt
1 tsp Vanilla Extract', '1. Preheat the oven to 325 F and line a baking sheet with parchment paper
2. Whip the two egg whites in a bowl on medium speed till soft peaks form - that means when you lift the whisks out from the batter it will form peaks
3. Combine the remaining ingredients in a bowl and mix in the egg whites. The batter will be thick and very heavy on the coconut
4. Scoop 1 inch balls onto a cookie sheet placing them 2 inches apart.
5. Bake for 20-25 minutes until they are a golden colour - mine were done at 23 minutes. You can also freeze these cookies after they have been baked and defrost for a few hours at room temperature whenever you want to eat them.', 13, 0.89, 1.16, 0.43, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/coconut-macaroons-with-unsweetened-coconut/'),
('Apple Snack Cake', NULL, 'A sweet tender quick bake that is difficult to resist!', '1 cup chopped apples
6 tbsp butter (85g) (room temperature)
1 cup sugar
2 eggs
1 tsp vanilla extract
1/2 cup buttermilk ((see notes))
1 1/2 cup all purpose flour
1 1/2 tsp baking powder
1/2 tsp baking soda
1/2 tsp salt
1/2 tsp cinnamon ((3/4 if you like stronger cinnamon flavour))
1/4 tsp ground cardamom ((optional, but highly recommended))
1/2 tbsp coarse sugar
pinch of cinnamon', '1. Lightly Grease a 9*9 pan and preheat your oven to 350 F
2. Mix the dry ingredients in a bowl and set aside
3. Beat the butter and sugar until it''s well combined, 2-3 minutes
4. Add the eggs one by one, beat for a minute between each addition
5. Now add in the Vanilla Extract, beat for 30 seconds
6. Mix in the dry ingredients alternately with the milk until just combined. Do not over beat!
7. Fold in the chopped apples
8. Spread the batter out in your pan
9. Mix the coarse sugar and cinnamom together and sprinkle over top
10. Bake for 22-26 minutes, start checking on the cake at the 22 minute mark, a skewer inserted in the middle will come out clean.', 143, 2.22, 22.52, 5.1, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/apple-snack-cake-of-my-dreams/'),
('Gobi Chicken', NULL, 'A chicken and cauliflower stew that is decidedly unusual but incredibly delicious and perfect with some hot roti!', '3/4 lb Boneless Chicken cut into 1.5 inch cubes
1/4 cup oil
1/2 tsp Cumin Seeds
1/2 cup Onion (1 medium) (finely diced)
1 tsp Garlic Paste
1/2 tsp Ginger Paste
1/2 tsp Coriander Powder
1/2 tsp Cumin Powder
1/2 tsp Turmeric Powder
1/2 tsp red chilli powder
1 tsp Salt
4-5 whole green chilies
2 - 2.5 cups Cauliflower Florets - half a large cauliflower or one small one
2 inch piece of ginger, cut into matchsticks
1/2 cup Scallions, green parts only
1/3 cup chopped cilantro
freshly cracked black pepper
lemon juice, just a squeeze for seasoning', '1. Heat a pan and add a generous lug of oil (about 1/4 cup)
2. Add the cumin seeds to the pan and when they sizzle add the diced onions
3. Once the edges of the onion start to turn golden brown then add the ginger and garlic paste
4. Stir and then add all the dry spices and salt.
5. Saute for a minute and then add the chicken
6. Keep cooking the chicken on medium high heat, stirring to ensure that the colour changes and the chicken starts to look cooked.
7. Add the green chilies and a cup of water to the pan.
8. Bring to a boil and then simmer with a lid on for about 25 minutes.
9. The chicken should be cooked through but not quite tender.
10. Gently mix in your cauliflower florets, cover and cook for another 10-12 minutes or until they''re just fork tender, not mushy.
11. Taste, adjust seasoning.
12. Now add the remaining ingredients - the scallions, ginger, cilantro, a few grinds of pepper and a squeeze of lemon juice.
13. Turn the stove off and let sit for a few minutes before serving with some Roti or Naan.', 370, 19.3, 15.52, 27.33, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/gobi-chicken-pakistani/'),
('Sesame Fried Chicken', NULL, 'a fun snack you can mix together in a bowl and fry up!', '1.5 lb boneless chicken cut into small 1.5 inch strips
1 tbsp soy sauce
1/2 tsp white pepper
1/4 tsp ginger paste
1/4 tsp garlic paste
1/3 cup cornstarch for super crispy or fill 1/3 cup halfway with flour and halfway with cornstarch
1/3 cup sesame seeds
1/4 tsp baking powder', '1. Mix the marinade up in a bowl, add the chicken pieces, stir to coat well and set aside for 20 minutes or longer
2. Whisk an egg and add it into the bowl, mix well.
3. Add remaining batter ingredients and mix, if the mixture becomes too sticky add a small splash of water
4. Heat oil in a saucepan, at least one inch of oil is ideal
5. When it starts to shimmer add the chicken pieces in one by one, making sure to shake any excess batter off into the bowl
6. Fry two minutes on each side until golden brown
7. Eat hot with your favourite condiment', 490, 34.62, 11.92, 33.31, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/sesame-fried-chicken-2/'),
('Pakistani Chinese Beef Chilli Dry', NULL, 'A Hakka style Beef Chilli Stir fry recipe that packs a strong flavour punch [Serving count estimated at 6 (main course, family-size) -- source recipe didn''t list servings; verify before treating as exact.]', '1 lb thinly sliced beef strips
1/2 tsp salt
1/2 tsp white pepper
1 tbsp soy sauce
1 egg white whipped
1 tsp oil
2 cloves garlic (crushed or minced)
2 Green Pepper, cut into strips
4-6 Green Chillies, cut into strips
1 tbsp soy sauce
1/2 tsp white pepper
1/2 tbsp vinegar
Oil for cooking', '1. Marinade the beef strip in the marinade ingredients for thirty minutes
2. Pour a lug of oil into a hot wok and stir fry the garlic till it starts to sizzle and change coloue
3. Now stir fry the beef, I like to get nice caramelly bits
4. Keep moving the beef around in the wok so it doesn''t stick together, it cooks fairly quickly
5. Add the strips of green pepper and chillies as well as the remaining ingredients, stir fry on high for 2-3 minutes, taste, adjust seasoning if needed with vinegar, pepper and soy. (I always add more!)', 215, 14.61, 1.75, 16.3, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/beef-chilli-dry-pakistani/'),
('Walnut Crumb Cake', NULL, '[Serving count estimated at 10 (whole cake/pie, sliced) -- source recipe didn''t list servings; verify before treating as exact.]', '2 tbsp butter
1/2 cup brown sugar
2 tbsp flour
1/2 cup walnuts or pecans (chopped)
1/2 tsp cinnamon
1/8 tsp salt
1/2 cup butter (room temp)
3/4 cup brown sugar
2 eggs
1 tsp vanilla extract
1.5 cup flour
2 tsp baking powder
1/2 tsp salt
1/2 cup milk', '1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F, grease a square cake dish - mine is 8**
2. Cut the butter into small pieces and combine it with the remaining ingredients in a small bowl, crumbling the mix together with your fingers. Refrigerate till ready to use
3. Stir together your flour, baking powder and salt in a small bowl. Set aside
4. Cream the brown sugar and butter together till creamy and fluffy - 3 to 4 minutes
5. Add eggs one by one, mixing 30 seconds between each addition
6. Now add in the vanilla, mix till combined
7. With the mixer on low alternately add the dry ingredients and milk, mix until combined. Be sure to scrape the bottom and side of your bowl.
8. Spread the batter into your prepared cake tin and then scatter the refrigerated crumb topping on top.
9. Bake for 30 minutes or until a skewer inserted in the middle comes out clean.', 350, 4.96, 43.89, 17.94, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/walnut-crumb-cake/'),
('Quick Whole Wheat Chocolate Muffins', NULL, NULL, '1 3/4 cup all purpose flour or whole wheat pastry flour
2 tsp baking powder
1/4 tsp baking soda
3/4 cup brown sugar
1/2 cup cocoa
1 cup milk
1/2 cup oil (any neutral flavour)
1/2 tsp vanilla extract
2 eggs
1/4 cup chocolate chips (optional)', '1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F
2. Put paper liners in your muffin cups or lightly grease your muffin tray
3. Whisk the dry ingredients in a medium to large bowl
4. Measure the oil and milk into a measuring cup, add the remaining wet ingredients to it and whisk well
5. Stir the wet ingredients into the dry ones until well combined, small lumps are ok.
6. Add the chocolate chips if using.
7. Fill each muffin cup a little over 2/3 of the way full
8. Bake for 16 to 20 minutes or until a toothpick inserted in the middle comes out clean', 202, 2.8, 22.48, 11.68, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/quick-whole-wheat-chocolate-muffins/'),
('Kid Friendly Instant Pot Pulled Beef for EVERYTHING', NULL, '[Serving count estimated at 6 (no keyword match, generic main-dish default) -- source recipe didn''t list servings; verify before treating as exact.]', '1 lb beef cubes
1/2 tsp ginger
1/2 tsp garlic
1 tbsp soy sauce
2 tsp sambal oelek (can add more)
2 tsp oil', '1. Add all the ingredients to the IP with 2 cups water, give it a good stir and put it on Manual (high pressure) for 20 minutes.
2. Let the IP natural release or manually vent it after ten minutes, the meat should be super tender.
3. Saute and stir to dry up the liquid a little. Done.', 207, 13.24, 0.42, 16.65, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/kid-friendly-instant-pot-pulled-beef-for-everything/'),
('15 Minute Shrimp and Coconut Curry', NULL, '[Serving count estimated at 6 (main course, family-size) -- source recipe didn''t list servings; verify before treating as exact.]', '1 onion, extra finely diced
1/4 t tsp kalonji (onion/nigella seeds)
1 sprig curry leaves
1 400 ml can coconut milk
1/2 tsp ginger paste
1/2 tsp garlic paste
3/4 - 1 tsp salt
1 tsp red chilli powder
1/8 tsp turmeric powder
3-4 tbsp tomato paste
a pinch of sugar
200g peeled raw shrimp
2-3 green chillies cut into strips (optional)', '1. Heat a little oil in a heavy bottomed pot
2. Add the nigella seeds, let them splutter a little then add the onions
3. Saute the onions until just translucent and then add the garlic and ginger paste, cook for a minute
4. Now add the chilli powder, turmeric, and 3/4 tsp salt
5. Cook till the oil rises a little to the top then add curry sprig and 3 tbsp of the tomato paste, stir to mix
6. Pour in the coconut milk, a pinch of sugar, mix well and bring to a boil.
7. Add the shrimp, let cook just until the shrimp forms a open C shape.
8. Adjust consistency with water per your liking ( I usually add a small splash) then taste and add more tomato paste if needed and the green chillies (if using)
9. Serve with plain rice', 49, 7.34, 3.29, 1.04, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/15-minute-shrimp-and-coconut-curry/'),
('A Crunchier Lahori Fried Fish', NULL, '[Serving count estimated at 6 (main course, family-size) -- source recipe didn''t list servings; verify before treating as exact.]', '2 lb any white firm fish cut into 2 inch pieces
3/4 tsp garlic paste
3 tbsp lemon juice
3/4 tsp salt
2.5 tbsp whole coriander seeds
1.5 tbsp ajwain (caraway seeds)
1 tbsp kasuri methi / fenugreek leaves (heaped)
1 1/2 tbsp cumin seeds
2-3 tbsp red chilli flakes
1/2 tsp red chilli powder (cayenne)
1/3 tsp turmeric powder
1/4 tsp black salt (optional)
2 tbsp besan/ chickpea flour
1 1/2 tbsp breadcrumbs
Chaat Masala
Lemon Wedges
Tartar Sauce
Oil (for frying)', '1. Squeeze the lemon juice over the fish, sprinkle w a little salt (not included in ingredients), add the garlic paste and mix deftly.
2. Coarsely grind the coriander seeds, cumin seeds, and ajwain in a grinder (4-5 seconds) and add to the fish along with the rest of the spices and the methi
3. Set aside for 20 minutes
4. Heat an inch or more of oil in a pan.
5. When the oil starts to shimmer then mix the breadcrumbs and besan into the fish to give good coverage. If the mixture is too dry then add a splash of water, but not too much. You want the mixture to stick to the fish, but not become gummy. If it does become gummy then add a little more besan and breadcrumb
6. Test fry a piece of fish 3 minutes on each side, adjust seasoning if needed.
7. Continue frying the fish in batches and drain on paper towels.
8. Serve right away with tartar sauce, wedges of lemon and chaat masala on the side', 194, 27.92, 8.5, 6.11, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/a-crunchier-lahori-fried-fish/'),
('Pineapple Upside Down Cake', NULL, 'Moist, tender Pineapple Upside Down Cake! [Serving count estimated at 10 (whole cake/pie, sliced) -- source recipe didn''t list servings; verify before treating as exact.]', '200 g pineapple slices (about 2-2.5 cups cubed or half a cored pineapple)
4 tbsp butter melted and cooled
1/2 cup brown sugar
pinch of salt
1 2/3 cup flour
1 1/2 tsp baking powder
1/4 tsp baking soda
1/2 tsp salt
1 stick butter (half a cup at room temperature)
2/3 cup sugar
2 eggs
2/3 cup milk
1 tsp vanilla extract or a few drops lemon or orange extract', '1. Preheat the oven to 350 F
2. Spread the melted butter on the bottom of the pan and use a brush or clean fingers to grease the sides as well
3. Sprinkle the brown sugar over the butter
4. Arrange pineapple chunks or slices. I cut my slices about 1/4 inch thick.
5. Cream room temp butter and sugar till light and fluffy.
6. Add the eggs one by one, beat for about a minute after each addition.
7. Pour in the extract you are using and beat for another 30 seconds.
8. Alternately mix in your dry ingredients and milk in 2-3 batches just until the ingredients are used up and a cohesive batter is formed.
9. Bake for 40-45 minutes depending or until a toothpick inserted in the middle comes out clean.
10. Cool for 10-15 minutes before inverting on to your serving plate.
11. Absolutely divine warm.', 247, 3.99, 43.23, 6.65, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/pineapple-upside-down-cake/'),
('Kurkuri Bhindi - 3-Ingredient Crunchy Okra', NULL, '[Serving count estimated at 4 (side dish/snack) -- source recipe didn''t list servings; verify before treating as exact.]', '- Pakistani/Indian Okra
- Chaat Masala
- Oil', '1. - Heat oil in a wide bottomed pan or wok, you want a generous lug for stir frying
2. - Stir fry the okra on high heat moving periodically to make sure it cooks evenly and doesn''t burn.
3. - Remove with a slotted spoon and put on paper towels to drain the extra grease
4. - Season with Chaat Masala, toss to mix and serve immediately.', 5, 0.03, 0.1, 0.5, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/crispy-3-ingredient-bhindi-okra/'),
('Spicy Whole Roasted Cauliflower', NULL, '[Serving count estimated at 4 (side dish/snack) -- source recipe didn''t list servings; verify before treating as exact.]', 'One head cauliflower
2 tbsp olive oil
2 tbsp lemon juice
1 tbsp garlic paste
1/2 tbsp salt
1/2 tbsp red chilli powder
Half teaspoon turmeric powder
A half inch piece of fresh ginger
1/2 tsp whole black peppercorns
1/2 tsp cumin seeds', '1. Combine all the ingredients in the garlic spice paste
2. Trim the leaves off the cauliflower and cover it with the garlic spice paste
3. Roast at 425 for 45 minutes, insert a skewer to check doneness, it should go through fairly easily.
4. While the cauliflower is roasting use a mini grinder (like a magic bullet) or mortar and pestle to crush the ingredients for the ginger paste without adding any water.
5. Sprinkle the ginger mix over the cauliflower at the 45 minute mark (assuming it is fairly tender) and roast for another ten minutes.
6. Serve as a beautiful side to any rice dish!', 95, 1.55, 7.18, 7.39, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/spicy-whole-roasted-cauliflower/'),
('Aaloo Gajar ki Sabzi - Spicy Potatoes & Carrots', NULL, 'A simple flavorful veggie dish that goes so well with all flat breads [Serving count estimated at 4 (side dish/snack) -- source recipe didn''t list servings; verify before treating as exact.]', '1 large or 2 small carrots
2 yukon gold potatoes
4-6 green chillies (halved)
1/2 tsp nigella seeds/ kalonji
2/3 tsp salt
oil for cookin', '1. Cut the veggies in a similar dice - thicker matchsticks/ slim french fries is my preferred shape.
2. Heat a glug of oil in a large bottomed pan on medium high heat.
3. Add the seeds and when they start to splutter then add the carrots and half the salt, mix well. Cover and cook on low heat for 10-12 minutes until the carrots are tender crisp.
4. Now add the potatoes and the remaining salt and cook for another 8-10 minutes till the potatoes are almost done.
5. Add the slit green chillies, mix well, and cook, covered, for five minutes. Adjust seasoning if needed.', 71, 2.25, 14.46, 0.72, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/aaloo-gajar-a-simple-potato-and-carrot-dish/'),
('Pakistani Soya Aloo ki Sabzi', NULL, 'A quick everyday dish that is brightened up with dill! [Serving count estimated at 4 (side dish/snack) -- source recipe didn''t list servings; verify before treating as exact.]', '3-4 small to medium sized potatoes ((chopped it will be about 3 cups))
canola oil for cooking
3-4 whole dried red chillies
1/2 tsp cumin seeds
3/4 tsp crushed chilli flakes
1 tsp salt
1/2 cup washed and chopped dill (fresh)', '1. Peel the potatoes, cut into large wedges and then dice those into 1/2 cm thick slices. If you prefer to cut them another way that is fine too
2. Heat oil in a pan on medium heat. A wider skillet will allow for quicker cooking but a small 7-8 inch one is fine too
3. Add the cumin seeds and whole red chillies. When the cumin seeds crackle turn down the heat a little and add the chilli flakes. The oil will turn a lovely red.
4. Now in go the potatoes and salt, give it all a little whirl and let the potatoes cook for 20 minutes on low heat. Do not add water.
5. When the potatoes are done taste, adjust seasoning and then add the chopped dill. Gently stir and cover the pot. Turn the stove off, let sit for a few minutes then eat.', 88, 2.2, 18.7, 0.82, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/pakistani-soya-aloo/'),
('Chili Garlic Noodles', NULL, 'Quick fix, week day friendly chili garlic noodles for the win.', '400 g the widest slurpiest noodles - a wide rice noodle or a tagliatelle etc.
3 tbsp olive oil
2 tbsp garlic, minced (8 cloves of garlic)
2 tbsp ginger, minced (2 inch piece of ginger)
2-3 tbsp soy sauce
1/4 cup scallions (green parts, roughly 2)
1/4 cup cilantro, chopped
1 tbsp chili flakes (or to taste)
additional soy sauce or salt for adjusting seasoning', '1. Boil the pasta in salted water as per package instructions and make sure to reserve half a cup of pasta water
2. Warm the oil in a pan and when it starts to shimmer add your garlic, ginger, ginger, chili flakes, scallions, and cilantro.
3. Let it sizzle on medium heat for just a minute and then add 2 tbsp of soy sauce
4. Mix the pasta well, adding additional pasta water as needed to create a sauce and adjust seasoning with additional soy, salt, and pepper and dig in.', 487, 7.75, 86.48, 11.09, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/chili-garlic-noodles/'),
('Southwest Rolls', NULL, 'Crispy rolls with a zesty creamy filling that is SO satisfying!', '10 Spring Roll Wrappers
1/4 cup corn kernels (canned or frozen)
1/4 cup red pepper (finely chopped)
1/4 cup black beans
1/4 cup shredded chicken
3 tbsp scallions (sliced)
1/2 jalapeno deseeded or 1 small thai chili seeds scraped out (minced)
1/2 tsp coriander powder
1/2 tsp cumin powder
1/2 tsp chili powder
1/2 tsp garlic powder
1/2 tsp dried oregano
1/4 tsp salt
1/4 tsp pepper
4 oz cream cheese (half a block)
3-4 tbsp milk
olive oil for cooking and spraying/brushing on the rolls
3 tbsp flour + 2 tbsp water', '1. Sauté the jalapenos and peppers in a tbsp of oil, then add the black beans and corn followed by the spices and then the cream cheese
2. Mix well to make sure the cream cheese melts and stir in the chicken
3. Add milk to adjust consistency - mixture will be thick
4. Stir in scallions and let it come to room temperature
5. Once cooled then form spring rolls (see post)
6. Use the flour/water paste to seal the edges if you aren''t air frying
7. Spray the rolls with oil and air fry at 390F for 4 minutes on each side', 130, 4.0, 15.48, 6.4, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/southwest-rolls-air-fryer/'),
('Instant Pot Salan Masala', NULL, 'How to batch cook a curry base that will save you time!', '2-3 cinnamon sticks
1 tsp cloves
1 tsp whole black pepper
1 tsp cumin seeds
3 lb onions - roughly 7/8
3 tbsp garlic paste
3 tbsp ginger paste
1.5 tbsp salt
1 - 1.5 tbsp red chilli powder
2 tsp coriander powder (optional)
1 tsp turmeric powder', '1. Slice or dice your onions. Use a food processor or a mandolin if you have one handy.
2. Heat a generous amount of oil in your IP on saute mode.
3. When it is hot add the whole spices and saute for 30 seconds
4. Add the onions, keep stirring and cook for about 10 minutes until the edges/tips of most of the onions are slightly golden. For a darker curry base keep cooking (and stirring) for 15-20 minutes - usually it is safer to go for a light golden.
5. Now add your ginger and garlic pastes and saute for 2 minutes
6. Once they pastes are incorporated add the remaining dry masala and salt and saute until the mix starts to come together and form a cohesive paste. If it starts to burn add a small splash of water. When it is done the oil will rise to the top.
7. Pour 2.5 cups of hot water into the Instant Pot, give it a stir and put it on manual (pressure) for 20 minutes.
8. Let it naturally release and saute to reduce the liquid for a more concentrated base. If you want you can use an immersion blender to puree it at this point.
9. When it is cool enough to handle then drain the extra oil out of the masala
10. This mix will keep in the coldest part of your fridge for 10 days or you can freeze it into roughly one cup servings for 3 months.', 50, 1.46, 11.34, 0.43, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/instant-pot-salan-masala-2/'),
('Maple Pecan Cake', NULL, '[Serving count estimated at 10 (whole cake/pie, sliced) -- source recipe didn''t list servings; verify before treating as exact.]', '6 tbsp butter (room temp)
3/4 cup sugar
2 eggs
1 1/3 cup all purpose flour
1 tsp baking powder
1/4 tsp baking soda
1/2 tsp salt
1/3 cup buttermilk (or regular full fat milk)
1/3 cup maple syrup
1 tsp vanilla
1/3 cup chopped pecans
2.5 tbsp maple syrup
1 tbsp all purpose flour
2 tbsp additional maple syrup (optional)', '1. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F and prep a 9*5 loaf tin by greasing it, dusting with flour and tapping out the excess.
2. Dry roast the pecans in a small saucepan on medium heat, moving them around until they darken and smell toasty
3. Add the maple syrup and cook, stirring frequently until it is fully absorbed into the nuts
4. Remove from the saucepan immedately and on to a clean board or piece of parchment paper and let cool.
5. Toss with 1 tbsp of all purpose flour before adding to the cake to prevent sinking.
6. Whisk the flour, baking powder, baking soda and salt together in a small bowl and set aside
7. Measure your maple syrup, milk and vanilla extract directly into a measuring cup and set aside
8. Beat the butter and sugar on medium speed till fluffy and well combined
9. Add the eggs one by one beating for about a minute after each addition
10. With the mixer on low add half the flour, then the wet ingredients in your measuring cup then the remaining flour and mix until just combined. DO NOT over mix!
11. Now gently fold in most of your maple pecans - reserve some for the top.
12. Pour the batter into your prepared cake tin, scatter the remaining pecans on top
13. Bake for 35-45 minutes, mine was completely done at 35, a skewer inserted in the middle should come out clean
14. Let cool in the tin for 5 minutes then invert on to a plate and drizzle with additional maple syrup if desired.
15. The cake keeps well tightly wrapped and at room temperature for up to 4 days and tastes even better the day after it is made.', 287, 3.69, 42.58, 11.67, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/maple-pecan-cake/'),
('Box Patties with Chicken and White Sauce', NULL, '[Serving count estimated at 6 (main course, family-size) -- source recipe didn''t list servings; verify before treating as exact.]', '24 samosa wrappers or 12 egg roll wrappers
2 tablespoons butter
1 1/2 cup milk
3 tablespoons flour
3/4 cup shredded chicken (cooked)
1/2 cup finely minced onion
1/4 cup corn
2 tablespoons grated carrots
2 minced green chillies
a grating (small pinch of nutmeg)
Salt
Pepper
Oil for pan frying
Additional flour and water to create a ''glue'' for the wrappers', '1. * Put a 8-inch saucepan over medium heat and melt the butter
2. * Add in the flour, stirring so that the butter coats the flour as it darkens and takes on a nutty aroma
3. * Slowly add the milk whisking briskly to combine
4. * Once the milk is in add the remaining ingredients and stir frequently till the sauce becomes nice and thick.
5. *Check for seasoning - you want to make sure it is well seasoned
6. * Mix a tbsp of flour with two of water and stir well
7. * Lay a strip of the samosa wrapper down, put a dab of flour water in the middle and place another strip on top (like a plus sign). Place a dollop of the chicken mix in the centre and fold over to shut, sealing with additional flour and water.
8. * Once you are done then shallow fry them to golden brown crispness and serve hot.', 328, 9.4, 28.83, 19.62, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/chicken-white-sauce-squares/'),
('Bhindi ki Sabzi', NULL, 'Simple okra dish with a few spices and lovely flavor! [Serving count estimated at 4 (side dish/snack) -- source recipe didn''t list servings; verify before treating as exact.]', '1 lb Okra
3-4 dried whole red chillies
½ tsp cumin seeds
½-3/4 red chilli flakes
3/4-1 salt
Oil for cooking (a little less than ¼ cup)', '1. Slice the okra into 1/2 cm coins.
2. Heat oil in a saucepan, when it shimmers add the cumin seeds and dried whole red chillies
3. Add the the salt and the chilli flakes to the oil, then add the okra and stir deftly to coat well.
4. Cook uncovered on medium heat, stirring it every 5-6 minutes, the bhindi will darken, and cook through in 15-18 minutes for soft tender bhindi.
5. For a darker bhindi with more of a chew turn the heat up and saute a few more minutes until it''s to your desired doneness. Adjust seasoning.', 47, 2.43, 9.29, 0.85, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/bhindi-ki-sabzi-or-spicy-pakistani-style-okra/'),
('Pakora Mix & How to Make Pakoras', NULL, 'an all purpose pakora mix that you can premix and keep! [Serving count estimated at 6 (main course, family-size) -- source recipe didn''t list servings; verify before treating as exact.]', '4 cups besan
1 tbsp salt
1 tbsp chilli flakes
1 tbsp chilli powder
1 tbsp coriander powder
1 tbsp cumin seeds
1 tbsp cornstarch
1 tsp ajwain (optional)
1/2 tsp baking soda', '1. Combine all the dry ingredients in a clean air tight jar, they will easily last two weeks or more.
2. To make pakoras - take out some of the dry mix.For plain pakoras put 3/4 the amount of water to the dry mix and fry on medium heat till golden and for vegetable ones start with half a cup water to 1 cup mix and adjust if needed.
3. Tip: Draining your pakoras on a wire rack (versus paper towel) will lead to a crispier pakora!', 332, 18.71, 50.13, 6.34, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/5-ramadan-prep-tips-for-your-busy-life/'),
('Donna Hays Chocolate Meringue Cake', NULL, '[Serving count estimated at 10 (whole cake/pie, sliced) -- source recipe didn''t list servings; verify before treating as exact.]', '240 G Dark Chocolate (chopped)
180 G 3/4 cup Unsalted Butter, chopped
2 Eggs
4 Eggs (extra, yolks and whites seperated.)
½ cup Brown Sugar
1 tsp Vanilla Extract
⅓ CUP 50G Flour (sifted)
½ tsp Baking Powder
⅓ cup 40G Almond Meal (Ground Almonds)
1 cup 220G sugar
1 tsp white vinegar
3 tsp cornflour/cornstarch (sifted)
¼ cup 25G Dutch Cocoa (sifted) + additional for dusting', '1. Preheat oven to 325 degrees.
2. Lightly grease a 9 inch springform cake tin, line the base with parchment paper and set aside.
3. Melt the chocolate and butter together in a saucepan and let it cool a little.
4. Whisk the eggs, extra egg yolks, brown sugar and vanilla for 3–4 minutes or until pale and thick. Add the chocolate mixture, flour, baking powder and almond meal and fold gently to combine. Be thorough though!
5. Pour the cake mix into the tin and bake for 35-40 minutes.
6. Take the cake out of the oven and increase the temperature to 350.
7. Beat the egg whites in a clean bowl on high speed until soft peaks form and then gradually add the sugar whisking till it dissolves.
8. Now in goes the vinegar. Mix for another 2–3 minutes. The meringue will be thick and glossy. Fold through the cornflour and cocoa (don''t forget to sift both!) and gently spread the meringue onto the cake.
9. Bake for another 20–25 minutes or until the meringue is golden and crisp.
10. Let the cake cool at room temperature for 30 minutes and then run a knife between the cake and pan to loosen the sides. Remove the springform ring.
11. Refrigerate for two hours to meld the flavors together.
12. Serve at room temperature lightly dusted with cocoa powder.', 473, 6.29, 52.19, 27.08, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/chocolate-meringue-cake/'),
('Kharay Masalay ka Gosht', NULL, '[Serving count estimated at 6 (main course, family-size) -- source recipe didn''t list servings; verify before treating as exact.]', '1 lb beef boti
A medium onion sliced
1 1/2 tsp garlic paste
1 1/2 inch ginger grated or very very finely minced
3/4 tsp cumin seeds
1 inch cinnamon stick
1/2 tsp whole black pepper
6 cloves
2 black cardamoms
¾ ts salt
1 tsp chilli powder
1 tsp coriander powder
One third tsp turmeric powder
3/4 tsp Garam masala
1/2 tsp black pepper
1/2 cup yogurt - whipped and at room temp
green chillies & cilantro for garnishing
Neutral oil for cooking', '1. Heat a very generous glug of oil in a pot or pressure cooker
2. Add sliced onion
3. Fry till the edges are golden
4. Put the beef in the pot, saute and add the ginger and garlic
5. Add the whole spices, the red chilli powder, coriander powder, turmeric powder, and salt.
6. Cook till tender - for a pressure cooker add about a cup of hot water and cook till the meat is tender. For a regular pot add about a cup and a half, bring to a boil and simmer for 50 minutes to an hour until tender. Keep an eye on water levels to prevent burning!
7. Turn the heat up and dry up the water, when the masala is at the "right" level the oil will rise above the spice paste
8. At that point stir in the yogurt, the oil will quickly rise to the top.
9. Add diced chillies (according to taste), a handful of cilantro, black pepper and garam masala powder.
10. Give it a quick whirl and eat with roti!', 247, 14.92, 9.58, 16.8, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/kharay-masalay-ka-gosht/'),
('No Churn Caramel Crunch Ice Cream', NULL, '[Serving count estimated at 6 (churn batch) -- source recipe didn''t list servings; verify before treating as exact.]', '1/2 cup sugar
1/4 cup rice krispies
1/4 cup flaked or chopped almonds
note: you can use any nut to make the full 1/2 cup if you don''t have rice krispies!
2 cups whipping cream
300 ml dulce de leche + extra for drizzling (optional)
1 tsp vanilla extract', '1. Place the 1/2 cup sugar in a medium heavy based saucepan on medium heat
2. Line a baking sheet with parchment paper
3. Once the sugar starts to caramelize at the edges start watching it carefully, swirl the pan if needed to ensure even browning
4. When the caramel turns a deep amber in color then pull it off the heat, stir in the rice krispies and nuts and spread over your prepped baking sheet.
5. Wait for the caramel crunch to cool the break into pieces by hand
6. Whip the cream until fluffy and it holds peaks
7. Beat in the dulce de leche and vanilla
8. Stir in the caramel crunch pieces, reserving 1/3 for serving and scattering on top
9. Pour the ice cream mixture into a freezer safe container and scatter some of the crunch pieces on top.
10. Freeze for 6-8 hours or until firm.', 465, 5.58, 42.32, 31.28, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/no-churn-caramel-crunch-icecream/'),
('No Churn Coffee Toffee Ice Cream', NULL, '[Serving count estimated at 6 (churn batch) -- source recipe didn''t list servings; verify before treating as exact.]', '2 cups whipping cream
1.5 tbsp instant coffee
1 tbsp milk
1 can condensed milk
1/3 cup skor bits', '1. Warm the milk slightly, mix in the instant coffee granules and set aside.
2. Whip the cream till stiff peaks form
3. Fold in the condensed milk, coffee solution and half the skor bits.
4. Pour the ice cream mix into your container of choice, sprinkle more skor bits over top and freeze for 6+ hours.', 354, 7.12, 7.99, 33.27, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/no-churn-coffee-toffee-icecream/'),
('Vegetable Noodle Spring Rolls', NULL, '[Serving count estimated at 6 (main course, family-size) -- source recipe didn''t list servings; verify before treating as exact.]', '250 g noodles (boiled)
2 tbsp oil
2 cloves garlic (minced)
3 carrots (sliced)
1 bell pepper (sliced)
1 green chili (sliced)
1/2 cabbage (sliced)
4 spring onions (sliced)
2 tbsp soy sauce
2 tbsp sriracha sauce
1 tsp oyster sauce
1 tsp salt
1 tsp red chili flakes
1/2 tsp brown sugar
1 tsp crushed black pepper
1 tsp chicken powder (optional)
32 egg roll wrappers/spring roll sheets
1/4 cup all-purpose flour', '1. In a pan heat some oil and saute the minced garlic.
2. On high heat, fry the carrot and bell pepper. Don''t cook for more than 2 mins. You don''t want to lose the crunch.
3. Add the cabbage. Saute for a minute. Then toss in the green chilies and the noodles.
4. Then put in all your spices and sauces, keeping the heat on high. Toss around well.
5. Now add the spring onions and continue to stir. Dry any moisture and turn off heat. Put this filling in a bowl and let cool.
6. Make a thick paste with flour and water. This will be used to seal the spring rolls.
7. Take a sheet of spring roll. Put it in a shape of a diamond on your working surface. At one end add around 2 tbsp of the filling. Roll the corner over the filling, fold the two sides and roll tightly all the way up. Brush some flour paste on the edges to seal off.
8. Repeat for the rest of the filling. Keep all the spring rolls aside.
9. At this stage, you can freeze them in a single layer and when frozen transfer to a ziplock bag.
10. These spring rolls can be deep fried, shallow fried, air fried and even baked. I shallow fried them here. See air frying and baking instructions in the notes.
11. For frying, heat oil in your pot. Then fry these rolls on medium heat till golden on all sides.
12. Take out on a paper towel to drain excess oil.
13. Serve with your favourite chutney and enjoy!', 565, 42.96, 21.56, 33.44, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/vegetable-noodle-spring-rolls-from-chili-to-choc-feasting-with-friends/'),
('Chawal ki Kheer - Pakistani Rice Pudding', NULL, '[Serving count estimated at 6 (dessert/snack bowls) -- source recipe didn''t list servings; verify before treating as exact.]', '1/4 cup rice, soaked
1 litre whole milk
5-6 cardamom pods
10 tbsp sugar
1/4 - 1/2 cup cream (or half n half)', '1. Boil your rice until it is mushy - this is at least 10 minutes of active boiling
2. While that happens use a wide bottomed steel pot (NOT NON STICK) to bring your milk to a simmer
3. Lightly bruise the cardamom pods and add them to the milk, keep the temperature low,
4. Once the rice is mushy, drain most of the water and then mash it up thoroughly on a plate with a fork
5. Add to the milk mixture along with the sugar. Mix well.
6. Cook on low - a gentle simmer for an hour. The milk will scald at the bottom of the pan but should not burn. Stir with a rubber spatula every now and then to check.
7. The kheer will cook down quite a bit in this time, add 1/4 cup of the cream you are using and taste - add more sugar or cream if desired
8. Serve garnished with nuts or plain.', 217, 6.65, 35.28, 5.95, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/chawal-ki-kheer-pakistani-rice-pudding/'),
('Chicken Karahi Qeema', NULL, 'A stir fried chicken with tomatoes, ginger and chillies! [Serving count estimated at 6 (main course, family-size) -- source recipe didn''t list servings; verify before treating as exact.]', '1 lb ground chicken
1/2 tsp kalonji/ nigella seeds
1 tbsp ground garlic
1 tbsp ground ginger (minced is better if possible + a 1.5 inch piece cut into matchsticks for garnish)
4-5 to matoes finely diced
1 tsp salt
2-2.5 tsp red chilli powder
1.5 tsp coriander powder
1 tsp cumin powder
1 tsp garam masala powder
green chillies 3-6 sliced lengthwise
handful of chopped cilantro
a squeeze of lemon juice (optional)', '1. - Heat oil in a wok and add the nigella seeds
2. - When they start to splutter then add the minced/ground ginger and garlic
3. - Add the ground chicken and the spices and cook on high stirring frequently until the chicken is nicely browned (this is chicken though so it wont get dark like beef does)
4. - Add the tomatoes, mix well. For quicker cooking cover the dish for a few minutes, this will soften the tomatoes
5. - Uncover the dish and cook on high until the ''masala'' becomes dry and the oil starts to rise. If this is not happening at all you may need to add more oil.
6. - Add the garam masala, stir, check for seasoning.
7. - Turn off the flame. Garnish with the chillies, ginger, and cilantro. squeeze over a little lemon juice if using.', 183, 14.82, 3.97, 12.05, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/chicken-karahi-qeema/'),
('Chana Palak or Chholay Palak - Chickpea and Spinach Curry', NULL, 'A no tomato curry that comes together in less than 20 minutes for a satisfying nutritious weeknight meal.', '1/2 tsp cumin seeds
1/2 cup minced onions
1.5 tsp garlic
3/4 tsp grated ginger
1/2 tsp salt
1/2 tsp chilli powder (cayenne)
1/3 tsp turmeric
1/2 tsp cumin powder
1/2 bouillon/ stock cube
19 fl oz canned chickpeas (used PC Blue Menu Chickpeas)
2 cups chopped washed spinach
1/4 tsp freshly cracked black pepper
green chillies, cilantro for garnishing and extra flavour!', '1. Heat a lug of oil in a saucepan and when it starts to shimmer add the cumin seeds, they will crackle and smell delicious
2. Add the minced onion and cook just until the edges are golden brown
3. Now stir in the ginger and garlic and saute for a minute
4. Add in the remaining spices and saute for another minute
5. Now drain the can of chickpeas and add to the pot along with about 1.5 cup of hot water and your half a stock cube.
6. Bring to a boil and simmer for 15-20 minutes until the chickpeas reach desired tenderness.
7. Take off the stovetop and stir in the spinach, it will wilt instantly.
8. Top with your cilantro.
9. For greater heat remove kid sized portions and add some minced green chillies to the chickpeas or simply top with the chillies after plating
10. Goes well with rice and flatbreads.', 648, 36.76, 107.88, 10.53, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/cholay-palak-chickpea-and-spinach-curry/'),
('Cream Cheese Cucumber Rounds', NULL, 'Bright fresh cucumbers provide the perfect base for savory cream cheese filling! [Serving count estimated at 6 (no keyword match, generic main-dish default) -- source recipe didn''t list servings; verify before treating as exact.]', '8 oz Cream Cheese (room temp)
1/2 tsp dried oregano
1/2 tsp dried thyme
1/8 tsp dried dill
1 clove garlic, crushed or super finely minced
1/8 tsp black pepper
2 tbsp whipping cream
3 English Cucumbers (12-14 inches)
minced chives or parsley for garnishing', '1. Whip the cream cheese and all the filling ingredients except the cream until smooth
2. Add the cream and whip till the cream is well incorporated and the mixture looks fluffier - about 2 minutes
3. Wash your cucumbers well and peel alternate strips. You should see a peeled stripe, then a darker green one where the skin remains, etc
4. Cut into one inch thick rounds
5. Scoop out the centers of the cucumber with a melon baller or a small spoon to create an indent
6. Fill a piping bag with the cream cheese mixture - I used a large tip but you can also just cut a hole in the corner of a ziploc bag and pipe a pretty round
7. When they are all filled then garnish with parsley or chives. You can serve these immediately or efrigerate them for up to two hours but not much longer because they can get too watery depending on the cucumber.', 165, 1.99, 5.13, 15.61, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/cucumber-cream-cheese-rounds/'),
('Praline Cake', NULL, NULL, '1 1/2 cup all purpose flour
3/4 tsp baking powder
1/4 tsp baking soda
1/2 tsp salt
6 tbsp butter (room temp)
1 cup sugar
1 egg
1 egg yolk
2 tsp vanilla extract
3/4 cup buttermilk
3/4 cup brown sugar
1/2 cup butter
1/4 cup cream
1 tsp vanilla extract
pinch of salt
1 cup walnut or pecan pieces', '1. Preheat the oven to 375 degrees, grease and flour a 9 inch cake pan
2. Mix the flour, baking powder, baking soda and salt in a bowl and set aside.
3. Cream the butter and sugar together
4. Add eggs, beat for 1-2 minutes
5. Now add the vanilla and mix to combine
6. Alternatingly add the buttermilk and dry ingredients in 2 batches each until just mixed.
7. Pour into prepared pan and bake for 28-30 minutes or until a skewer inserted in the middle emerges clean
8. Put a frying pan on medium high heat, add your notes, toast the nuts, swirling every thirty seconds or so for about 2 minutes. They will darken and smell toasty.
9. Bring the brown sugar, butter and cream to boil in a small saucepan, simmer for 3 minutes and then add the vanilla and salt.
10. Stir in the nuts and pour over the cake.', 532, 4.03, 51.04, 35.38, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/deliciously-easy-buttermilk-skillet-cake-with-praline-topping/'),
('Garlicky Spinach and Potato Croquettes', NULL, 'Easy to make Garlicky Spinach and Potato Croquettes [Serving count estimated at 6 (main course, family-size) -- source recipe didn''t list servings; verify before treating as exact.]', '6 medium potatoes (boiled)
2 tbsp minced onion
2-3 cloves crushed garlic
1 tsp red chilli flakes
1/2 tsp cumin powder
1/4 tsp turmeric powder
salt
2 cups chopped spinach
1-2 tbsp butter
2 eggs
2 cups breadcrumbs', '1. Saute the minced onion in 2 tbsp of oil
2. Add the garlic and then saute for another 30 seconds before adding the remaining spices
3. Give it a quick stir then remove from the pan
4. Wilt your chopped spinach in the same pan and set aside
5. Mash your potatoes well with 1-2 tbsp butter (by preference)
6. Mix in the spice mix and the spinach and taste. Adjust seasoning.
7. Get a piping bag or a ziploc bag and cut a 3/4-1 inch hole in the tip. Fill your bag with the potato mix and pipe out 3 inch croquettes trimming with kitchen scissors as you go along.
8. Freeze for 30 minutes for easier handling.
9. Whip your eggs (seasoning optional) with a splash of water and put your breadcrumbs out in a plate
10. Roll each cutlet in egg wash and then breadcrumbs. Fry immediately for 2 minutes on each side till golden or freeze for another day.', 278, 9.78, 47.38, 6.1, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/garlicky-potato-spinach-croquettes-with-the-best-hack/'),
('Khageena', NULL, NULL, '4 eggs
1/4 cup minced onion
3-4 minced green chillies
salt
red chilli powder
oil for cooking
chopped cilantro for garnish (optional)', '1. Heat a lug of oil in a saucepan
2. Briskly whisk the eggs, a little chilli powder and a fat pinch of salt together
3. When the oil shimmers (gets hot) add your onions and green chillies and saute until the onion looks translucent
4. Add your eggs and cook, breaking and folding in on over itself till required doneness
5. Eat hot with toast', 168, 13.23, 4.18, 10.75, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/khageena/'),
('Desi Roast Turkey with Lahori Chargha Masala and Green Chutney', NULL, 'An Oven Roasted Turkey with the masala of a Lahori Chargha and the char of a beautiful barbecue, perfect for large crowds! [Serving count estimated at 12 (whole roast, gathering-size) -- source recipe didn''t list servings; verify before treating as exact.]', '12-14 lb Canadian Turkey
¾ cup kosher salt
¾ cup brown sugar
Enough water to completely submerge the turkey
150 g chargha masala
½ cup lemon juice
4 tbsp ginger
4 tbsp garlic
6 tbsp butter softened
½ cup + 1 cup yoghurt
¼ cup mint leaves
¼ cup cilantro leaves
½ clove garlic
¾ tsp red chilli powder
½ tsp cumin seed powder
5 green chillies
Salt', '1. Two days before roasting the turkey place the turkey in a large pot or container big enough to submerge it. Ensure that the giblets have been removed and the cavity is clean.
2. Warm a cup full of water and mix the brown sugar and salt into it. Add enough water to cover the turkey. Cover and set aside for 12-24 hours
3. Take the brined turkey out of the fridge, drain the brine and pat the Turkey dry.
4. Place the turkey in a dish – you can use the roaster you will roast it in as well.
5. Whisk the marinade ingredients except the butter in a bowl. Reserve the squeezed lemons for later.
6. Stir in your softened butter
7. Now with clean hands (or gloves) lift the skin at the bottom of the turkey breast, it will separate from the breast meat. Stuff about 1/5 of your marinade mixture into each breast half.
8. Shmear the rest over the back, legs, and wings of the turkey. If using butter it may not go on like a smooth even paste but that''s fine!
9. Spread any remaining marinade on top of the turkey breasts
10. Stuff the cavity with the juiced lemons.
11. Leave uncovered in the fridge.
12. The day you are going to roast the turkey pull it out of the fridge a few hours before roasting to bring it to room temperature
13. Preheat the oven to 450F, place the oven tray on the last rack.
14. Roast the Turkey till the top is a gorgeous brown colour, some of the masala will look charred and that is delicious. This will take about 30 minutes
15. Drop the temperature to 350 F, tent the turkey with foil and roast until a meat thermometer inserted in the thigh reads 170 degrees F, this took me another 1 hour and 50 minutes over and above the initial bake time.
16. Let the turkey meat rest for at least 20 minutes before carving.
17. Serve with the green chutney, parathas, and a simple sabzi pulao.
18. Blitz half a cup of yogurt, mint leaves, cilantro leaves, the salt, red chilli powder, green chillies, and garlic in a food processor till smooth. Pour into a bowl and whisk in an additional cup of yogurt.', 864, 98.11, 19.76, 44.09, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/my-desi-roast-turkey-with-lahori-chargha-masala-and-green-chutney/'),
('No Tomato Highway Chicken Karhai', NULL, '[Serving count estimated at 6 (no keyword match, generic main-dish default) -- source recipe didn''t list servings; verify before treating as exact.]', '1 lb Boneless chicken cut into bite size pieces
7-10 Green Chillies, sliced
1 tbsp Chopped Ginger
1/2 tbsp Chopped Garlic
Salt to taste
1 tsp Coarse Black Pepper
1 tbsp Lemon Juice
Oil/Ghee for Cooking
Handful of Coriander leaves
Julienned Ginger for Garnish
1/2 tbsp Coriander powder
1/2 tbsp Red Chilli Flakes
1/2 tbsp Cumin Seeds
1/2 tsp Kasoori Methi
1/2 tbsp Chaat Masala
1/2 tsp Khatai/Raw Mango Powder
1/4 tsp Black Salt
1/2 tsp Garam Masala Powder', '1. Dry roast the coriander seeds and cumin seeds in a pan until darker and aromatic, pulse a few times to coarsely grind. Mix in remaining Karhai Masala ingredients
2. Add the chopped ginger, garlic and green chillies to the oil, cook for 30 seconds and add the chicken pieces, salt and pepper.
3. Saute until ALL the pieces have changed color i.e. no longer look raw
4. Add a splash of water and cook on medium heat stirring often and when the chicken is almost done (test by breaking a piece) add the Karhai Masala, Lemon Juice and Julienne Ginger (if using) and stir fry for another minute.
5. Turn off the stove.
6. Cover the dish and heat a piece of coal on the stove top till you can see parts of it changing color. Put a piece of foil in your wok, place the coal on top, add a splash of oil and as soon as smoke billows from it shut the dish for at least five minutes
7. Top with chopped cilantro and serve immediately with your flatbread of choice', 187, 14.98, 4.3, 12.27, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/no-tomato-smoky-highway-karhai-chicken/'),
('Tandoori Oven Roasted Brussel Sprouts', NULL, 'A spicy roasted brussel sprouts recipe with big flavor [Serving count estimated at 6 (main course, family-size) -- source recipe didn''t list servings; verify before treating as exact.]', '1 lb brussel sprouts
1-1.5 tbsp Tandoori Masala Powder
Olive Oil for tray
sliced onions
chopped cilantro
lemon wedges', '1. Preheat the oven to 375, line a baking sheet with foil
2. Trim the tough outer leaves off the brussel sprouts and cut in half
3. Toss with the tandoori masala and a generous glug of olive oil
4. Bake for 8 minutes, take them out of the oven, toss gently. Bake for another 5-8 minutes or till done', 41, 2.64, 8.4, 0.57, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/oven-roasted-tandoori-brussel-sprouts/'),
('Salty-Sweet Butterscotch Chip Cookies Recipe', NULL, 'The ULTIMATE butterscotch cookies with the most fantastic addictive flavors!', '1 cup pecan halves
2/3 cup light brown sugar (firmly packed)
2/3 cup granulated sugar
1 cup butter
1/2 teaspoon salt
1/2 teaspoon espresso powder or 3/4 tsp instant coffee
1 teaspoon baking soda
2 teaspoons vanilla extract
1 teaspoon vinegar (cider or white)
1 large egg
2 cups All-Purpose Flour
1 1/3 cups butterscotch chips
1/3 cup granulated sugar mixed with 1 to 1 1/4 teaspoons salt (for topping**)', '1. Toast your pecans in a clean dry frying pan on medium heat, moving occasionally until they darken and smell toasted. Chop roughly.
2. Cream together butter, sugars, shortening, salt, espresso/coffee powder, baking soda, vanilla, and vinegar till smooth sweet magic happens.
3. Add the egg, beat till well combined.
4. With your mixer on low gradually add the flour
5. Stir in the chips and toasted nuts.
6. Refrigerate the dough for 2 hours to overnight unless you are in a rush
7. When it is time to bake line your baking sheet (or two sheets) with parchment paper and preheat to 375 degrees F.
8. Combine the sugar and salt and put in a bowl. Make the size of cookie you prefer and roll into a ball, let the cookie take a little sugar shower then transfer to the baking sheet and leave 2 inches between cookies.
9. Bake the cookies for 9-12 minutes depending on the size of the cookie and the kind of cookie you like. A longer bake time will give you a delightfully crunchy cookie, a shorter bake time where the edges are golden and the cookie is just cooked in the middle will result in a softer chewy cookie.', 180, 1.47, 26.15, 7.9, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/salty-sweet-butterscotch-pecan-cookies/'),
('Garlic Chutney', NULL, 'The best garlic chutney ever.', '2 heads of garlic - about 20-22 cloves
1 tsp red chilli flakes
1 tsp kashmiri red chilli powder/parika or cayenne
3/4 tsp salt
2-3 tbsp oil', '1. Crush the garlic in the way that works best for you. I use my garlic press, but you can mince it by hand or use a mortar & pestle. Just please don''t grind it to a paste!
2. Heat 2 tbsp of oil in a small frying pan on medium heat
3. Add the garlic and saute for a minute and turn the heat down. Add a little more oil if needed, but try to avoid it.
4. Add the chilli flakes, chilli powder/paprika, and salt.
5. Cook on low heat for 5 minutes or so watching carefully so that the garlic doesn''t burn. Add a little water if needed. Done.', 185, 4.89, 25.31, 8.93, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/sauteed-garlic-chutney/'),
('Shallots with Coconut and Tamarind', NULL, '[Serving count estimated at 4 (side dish/snack) -- source recipe didn''t list servings; verify before treating as exact.]', '1 tbsp coriander seeds
1/2 cup shredded coconut (unsweetened)
2 tsp chilli powder
12 oz Shallots (10-12 depending on size)
1 1/2 tsp salt (start w 3/4, see notes)
1/2 tsp turmeric
1 1/2 tbsp tamarind paste
1/2 tsp nigella seeds (kalonji)
1 sprig cury leaves
3-4 dried red chillies
oil for cooking
optional garnish: minced cilantro, sliced mild chillies', '1. Peel and halve the shallots.
2. Toast the coconut and coriander seeds on medium high heat in dry saucepan, the coconut will get beautifully golden, 2-3 minutes. Stir to avoid burning
3. Blend the first three ingredients to a paste using a little water. Set aside.
4. Put a lug of cooking oil in a 10 inch saucepan and heat.
5. Now in with the shallots, cook for 3-4 minutes on medium high heat until browned on the outside and slightly softened
6. Add salt (start w 3/4 tsp), 1/4 cup water (may need more if it starts to burn), and turmeric. Cook for another 5 minutes.
7. Now pour in your coconut paste and 1 tbsp of the tamarind pulp. Mix well and adjust seasoning by adding more salt or another 1/2 tbsp of tamarind pulp.
8. Transfer the shallots to the serving dish.
9. Heat a tbsp and a half of oil n a small saucepan and add the nigella seeds (kalonji), curry leaves, and dried red chilli. Fry for about 20 seconds then pour over the shallots. Toss gently.', 174, 3.01, 19.66, 11.3, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/shallots-with-tamarind/'),
('Spicy Chicken Enchiladas with Our Favourite Enchilada Sauce', NULL, 'Spicy savory Enchiladas that will warm you up in chilly months! [Serving count estimated at 6 (main course, family-size) -- source recipe didn''t list servings; verify before treating as exact.]', '3 tbsp neutral oil
1 1/2 tbsp flour
3 tbsp red chilli powder (cayenne)
2 cups chicken stock
1 1/4 cup tomato puree or 1 cup passata
1 1/2 tsp oregano
3/4 tsp cumin
1/4 tsp sugar
salt (as needed)
2 cups shredded cooked chicken
1 medium sized white onion or half a large one
1-2 diced jalapenos, seeded or otherwise (upto you)
1/2 cup Monterey Jack or Cheddar (or a combo)
1/4 cup sour cream
salt
pepper
10 corn tortillas
oil for greasing the pan
1 1/2 cup Cheese (same as above) for topping
1/2 cup chopped scallions
2 tbsp sour cream', '1. Heat oil in a pot, when it shimmers add the flour and cook for 1-2 minutes on medium, stirring frequently
2. Add red chilli powder and saute (turn your stoves exhaust on for this!) for 30 seconds
3. Now add the rest of the ingredients
4. Bring to a boil and simmer for 20 minutes, until the sauce has thickened and almost halved. Add salt if needed.
5. Finely dice your onion
6. Combine the remaining filling ingredients, season.
7. Preheat the oven to 375 degrees. Lightly grease oven an ovenproof dish (12*7) or use a parchment lined baking sheet
8. Heat Corn Tortillas in a little oil in a pan for 30-45 seconds if needed, I usually skip this step since mine are quite soft!
9. Put a few tbsp of filling down the middle of each tortilla, roll and place in the baking sheet seam side down. Repeat till all the enchiladas have been made
10. Pour half of the enchilada sauce over the dish making sure to evenly distribute it. You may add more if it is needed.
11. Top with shredded cheese and bake for 25-30 minutes until deliciously bubbly
12. Garnish with scallions and dollops of sour cream & serve with the extra Enchilada Sauce on the side', 564, 35.01, 16.02, 41.18, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/spicy-chicken-enchiladas-favourite-enchilada-sauce/'),
('Tandoori Turkey Pizza', NULL, 'Use Tandoori Masala to jazz up your Turkey leftovers and this pizza!', '1 sachet active dry yeast (2 1/4 tsp)
1 cup very warm water
1 tsp sugar
1 tsp salt
3/4 tsp oregano
2 1/2 cup flour
1 tbsp olive oil
3/4 cup cooked Turkey chopped into bite sized pieces
2 1/2 tbsp Tandoori or Tikka Masala Sauce
1/2 green pepper, sliced into small strips
325 g mozzarella cheese (half a large bar)
1/4 cup sliced red onion
1/2-3/4 cup pizza sauce
2 thinly sliced green chillies
red chilli flakes
1 tbsp melted butter', '1. Pour the one cup water in a bowl, add the sugar and then sprinkle the yeast over.
2. Set aside for a few minutes - it''ll look a little foamy. You can skip this step if you''re 100% sure your active dry yeast is fresh, but if not then I recommend activating the yeast.
3. Add the remaining ingredients and knead for a few minutes to combine well. Place in a lightly oiled bowl.
4. I like to cover it with a cloth and put in a warm space for fifteen minutes to make rolling it out easier.
5. prep the pan by laying down parchment paper, sprinkling on cornmeal or lightly greasing the pan.
6. Roll the dough out to desired shape - oblong for a baking sheet, round for a pizza pan, or even 2 9 inch pizzas (adjust quantities for toppings by increasing by 50%)
7. Preheat the oven to 425 degrees.
8. Top the pizza with the sauce, spreading evenly
9. Scatter half the cheese, all the toppings and the remaining cheese.
10. Bake for 15-20 minutes until the pizza is golden and bubbly, when it is almost done pull it out and lightly brush the crust with melted butter.', 537, 44.57, 66.62, 10.41, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/tandoori-turkey-pizza/'),
('Dhaba Dal or Chana Dal Fry', NULL, 'A roadside restaurant inspired punchy chanay ki daal that hits all the flavour notes and is simple to make!', '1 cup chana daal (cooked) (instructions in notes)
4 tbsp ghee + oil (I use 2 tbsp each, but you can adjust to liking)
1 tsp cumin seeds
1/2 cup diced onion
1.5 tbsp freshly minced ginger ((or 1 measuring tbsp paste))
1.5 tbsp freshly minced garlic ((or 1 measuring tbsp paste))
2 tomatoes, chopped
1 1/4 tsp salt
1 tsp red chili powder ((halve it for a less spicy dal))
1/2 tsp red chili flakes
2 tsp coriander powder (roasted preferred)
1/3 tsp turmeric
1/2-1 tsp garam masala
1/2 tsp freshly cracked pepper
2 tbsp lemon juice
2-3 green chilies (sliced)
3 tbsp chopped cilantro
other add ins: julienned ginger, chaat masala', '1. Heat your oil + ghee in a wide bottomed pan on medium high heat
2. Add your cumin seeeds and once they sizzle add in your onions
3. Cook, sauteing frequently until the edges take on a caramelly color.
4. Add in your ginger and garlic and saute for a minute
5. Now stir in your tomatoes, salt, chili powder + flakes, coriander powder, and turmeric.
6. Cover with a lid for two minutes then remove the lid and saute until the masala becomes cohesive looking and the oil rises over the tomato paste. Add a splash of water if it starts to stick/burn.
7. Stir in your daal followed by 1.5 cup water , bring to a boil, and let it simmer for 10 minutes. You want the daal to be completely tender and absorb the flavors. If it was a bit tough earlier then you may need more time here.
8. Adjust the consistency to your liking and then adjust seasoning. If you are adding more water here then remember to bring it a boil first before shutting the stove off.
9. Add your favorite finishing touches and dig in!', 213, 6.61, 23.73, 11.39, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/chanay-daal/'),
('Gobi Gosht - Beef & Cauliflower Stew', NULL, NULL, '1/2 A Head of Cauliflower approximately 2 1/2 cups chopped
1 lb Boneless Beef (cut into 1.5 inch chunks)
1 large onion
1 tomato
1 tsp garlic paste
1/2 tsp ginger paste
1 tsp salt
1 tsp red chilli powder (add an extra 1/2 if you really want it spicy!!)
1/2 tsp coriander powder
1/3 tsp turmeric
1/2 tsp cumin seeds
1 inch piece ginger
1/2 tsp cumin seeds
1/2 tsp whole black peppers
Juice of a lemon
2 tbsp Chopped Cilantro
2-4 Green Chillies (diced)', '1. Combine everything from the boneless beef through to the cumin seeds in a pot or a pressure cooker. If using a pot then add two cups of hot water, mix, bring to a boil then simmer for an hour. If using an Instant Pot cook for 18-20 minutes then quick release.
2. Crank up the heat and dry up the masala until it starts to stick then add a lug of oil and cook till the oil seperates from the masala.
3. Add the chopped cauliflowers and mix well.
4. Cover and cook on low until the cauliflower is almost tender, 10 - 12 minutes, add a splash of water if it starts to stick.
5. While the cauliflower is cooking grind the ginger, black pepper and cumin seeds in a grinder or a crush them in a mortar and pestle.
6. When the cauliflower is done sprinkle the ginger mix over and stir to disperse being careful not to mush the cauliflower.
7. Squeeze over a little lemon juice and topped with bright fresh cilantro and green chillies. Eat with any kind of roti,i.e. chapati, naan, paratha, etc.', 334, 21.09, 9.76, 23.37, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/gobi-gosht-a-meat-and-cauliflower-stew-for-the-soul/'),
('Instant Pot Tandoori Roast Chicken', NULL, 'A spicy impressive tandoori roast made easy (and in under 30 minutes) with an Instant Pot! [Serving count estimated at 6 (main course, family-size) -- source recipe didn''t list servings; verify before treating as exact.]', '1 Skinless Chicken (Whole), 5.5-7lbs
1 lb baby potatoes, or regular potatoes in big chunks
1/2 packet Shan Masala brand Tandoori Roast Chicken Masala
1/2 packet Shan Masala brand Lahori Chargha Masala
1 Lemon, juiced
1/2 tsp garlic paste
1/2 tsp ginger paste
Half cup yogurt
2 tbsp oil
1/4 cup finely minced cilantro
lemon wedges', '1. Wash the chicken, truss the bird or simply tie the legs together with kitchen twine.
2. Use a sharp knife to make slits in the chicken, at least 4 each per chicken breast plus a few in the leg and place in a large bowl
3. Mix all the marinade ingredients in a small bowl
4. Pour over the chicken and rub well, leave for at least an hour or overnight
5. When almost ready to cook take the chicken out of the fridge
6. Heat the oil in the instant pot on saute mode on high
7. When it shimmers take the marinated chicken out of the bowl letting excess marinade drip back in to the bowl and carefully place the chicken, breast side down, in the instant pot
8. After 2-2.5 minutes add the remaining marinade back into the pot and put the instant pot on manual (i.e. pressure) on high for 8 minutes.
9. When the timer beeps open the vent to release pressure and tip the potatoes in, mix a little to coat them in marinade
10. Put the instant pot back on pressure for another 8-10 minutes (depending on the size of chicken you are using) and then release the pressure. If you opt for a natural release you will get a super tender chicken, but mind you it may be difficult to get out of the pot!
11. The chicken is ready to eat but if you want a more caramelized look you can put it in an oven safe roasting dish and broil it or even turn the saute function on high until the potatoes and chicken take on a darker hue, about 5 minutes!', 102, 2.06, 13.16, 5.13, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/instant-pot-tandoori-roast-chicken-cooked-in-under-30-minutes/'),
('Prairie Girl Classic Vanilla Bean Buttercream', NULL, '[Serving count estimated at 18 (cake-frosting component, tbsp-size use) -- source recipe didn''t list servings; verify before treating as exact.]', '1 1/2 cup salted butter at room temp
6 oz cream cheese at room temp
2 tbsp whipping cream
1 tbsp vanilla bean paste or seeds from one pod or 2tsp VE
6 cups icing sugar', '1. Beat the butter, cream cheese, cream, vanilla of choice, and 3 cups of icing sugar till smooth, about 3 minutes
2. With the mixer on medium add the remaining icing sugar, a cup at a time for 4 minutes
3. Now crank up the speed and beat to luxurious fluffiness for about 3-4 minutes.
4. Makes 6 cups.', 331, 0.48, 40.32, 19.35, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/vanilla-bean-buttercream/'),
('5-Ingredient Nutella Brownies', NULL, 'Quick, Easy Nutella Brownies!', '1 13- oz jar Nutella
2 eggs
1/2 cup flour
1/2 tsp baking powder
coarse salt or sea salt for sprinkling', '1. Preheat your oven to 350 degrees.
2. Lightly grease a square pan/dish – you can use a 9*9 or an 8*8.
3. Crack the eggs into a bowl, whisk to break up the yolks, then briskly stir in the nutella till well combined
4. Fold in the flour and baking powder. Spread in your pan, sprinkle with coarse salt.
5. Bake for 22-26 minutes or until a toothpick inserted comes out almost clean. Please check on them around the 22 minute mark. The middle should look set. These are gooey brownies, so let cool before cutting!', 23, 1.17, 2.93, 0.63, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/5-ingredient-nutella-brownies/'),
('Sweet and Spicy Roasted Cashews w Ginger and Honey', NULL, '[Serving count estimated at 4 (side dish/snack) -- source recipe didn''t list servings; verify before treating as exact.]', '2 cups roasted cashews
1 1/2 tbsp freshly grated ginger
2-3 tbsp honey (see notes)
1 tbsp brown sugar
1 1/2 tbsp oil
1/2 - 3/4 tsp red chilli flakes
2 tbsp sesame seeds', '1. Preheat the oven to 350 and line a baking sheet with parchment paper
2. Whisk together all the ingredients except the cashews until you have a smooth sauce
3. Toss in the cashews and mix to coat
4. Spread out onto a baking sheet, bake 5 minutes move them around and bake another 2-3 minutes until they look caramelly and done
5. Let cool entirely before eating!!! They will taste even better!', 470, 12.27, 35.62, 34.4, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/sweet-and-spicy-roasted-cashews/'),
('Ghar ki Maash ki Daal or Daal Mash', NULL, '[Serving count estimated at 4 (side dish/snack) -- source recipe didn''t list servings; verify before treating as exact.]', '1 cup Maash ki daal (soaked for a few hours, preferably overnight)
1/2 tsp ginger paste
4-5 diced green chillies
1 inch ginger piece, julienned
1/2 thinly sliced onion
3-4 whole dried red chillies
neutral cooking oil', '1. Rinse your soaked daal and put it to boil with a generous amount of water, the ginger paste and a spoon full of salt
2. Once the daal is cooked, 20-30 minutes, drain the excess water and return the daal to the pot
3. Finely mince however many green chillies you feel comfortable using and add those along with the julienned ginger (if using) into the pot
4. Taste for salt, adjust seasoning.
5. Heat a generous lug of oil in a small frying pan and add the onions and whole red chillies
6. When the onions turns a beautiful caramelly brown then pour the baghaar/tadka over the maash ki daal. Eat with roti.', 159, 9.81, 27.95, 1.55, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/ghar-ki-maash-ki-daal/'),
('Sweet and Salty Peanut Butter Cookies', NULL, 'Chewy peanut butter cookies w M&Ms made extra special with a sweet-salty twist! [Serving count estimated at 16 (batch of individual pieces) -- source recipe didn''t list servings; verify before treating as exact.]', '1/2 cup butter
1/2 cup granulated sugar
1/2 cup brown sugar
1 egg
1/2 tsp vanilla extract
3/4 cup + 2 tablespoons peanut butter
1 1/3 cup flour
1/2 teaspoon baking soda
1/2 teaspoon salt
1/3 cup M&M baking bits (the color doesn''t ''bleed'' when baking or 1/2 cup chocolate chips or peanut butter chips)
2 1/2 tablespoon sugar
1 1/4 tsp salt', '1. Mix the flour, baking soda and salt in a bowl and set aside.
2. Beat the butter and sugars together till fluffy and creamy. This takes me about 5 minutes.
3. Add the egg, beat for a minute.
4. In goes the vanilla, beat till combined.
5. Add the dry ingredients and mix till just combined.
6. Fold in M&Ms with a spatula.
7. Let the dough rest covered in the fridge for a few hours or overnight.
8. Preheat the oven to 350 degrees & line a baking sheet with parchment paper
9. Mix the salt and sugar for topping in a bowl
10. Make 1-inch balls of dough with a spoon or cookie scoop and drop into the bowl, roll it gently to coat and place on the baking sheet.
11. Repeat till your sheet is full taking care to leave 2 inches between the cookies.
12. Bake for 10-13 minutes or until the edges are golden brown but the cookie is still very soft in the middle. The cookie will still be fragile.
13. Wait a few minutes and then carefully transfer the cookies to a cooling rack to cool all the way through.', 242, 1.72, 24.68, 15.6, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/sweet-and-salty-peanut-butter-cookies/'),
('Ferrero Rocher Brownies', NULL, '[Serving count estimated at 16 (batch of individual pieces) -- source recipe didn''t list servings; verify before treating as exact.]', '3/4 cup butter
1 pound bittersweet chocolate (coarsely chopped)
3/4 cup + 2 tbsp flour
5 large eggs (at room temp)
2 cups brown sugar
1/2 teaspoon salt
1 teaspoon vanilla
20 Ferrero Rocher Balls', '1. Preheat your oven to 350 and grease a 9*13 pan. You can also use a 8*8 square tin and a 5*7.
2. Melt the butter over low heat, then pull the pan off the stove and stir in the chopped chocolate until it melts
3. Beat the eggs, sugar, salt and vanilla on high for 4-5 minutes until the mix becomes pale and thick. When you lift the beaters out the batter should form a wide ribbon that folds back on itself and slowly dissolves on the surface.
4. With a light hand, fold the cooled chocolate into the eggs, followed by the flour.
5. Pour the batter into the prepared dish and smooth the top.
6. Line up your Ferrero Rocher nice and pretty.
7. Take a little batter and cover the top of the chocolate balls to protect the chocolate from burning.
8. Bake until the top looks slightly cracked 25-35 minutes (depending on pan)
9. Cool completely before cutting into squares', 401, 5.15, 47.79, 21.52, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/ferrero-rocher-brownies/'),
('Peanut Butter Blondies', NULL, '[Serving count estimated at 16 (batch of individual pieces) -- source recipe didn''t list servings; verify before treating as exact.]', '1 cup flour
1/2 tsp baking powder
1/4 tsp baking soda
1/4 tsp salt
1/2 cup peanut butter (not natural)
5 tbsp room temp butter
3/4 cup sugar
3/4 cup brown sugar
2 large eggs
1/2 tsp vanilla extract
1 cup chopped peanuts
2/3 cup milk chocolate chunks/chips
1/4 cup peanut butter chips (can use additional chocolate chips instead)', '1. Preheat your oven to 350 degrees and prep a square baking tin with parchment paper or buttered foil
2. Whisk the flour, baking powder, baking soda and salt together in a bowl and set aside.
3. Beat the peanut butter and butter together till luxuriously smooth
4. Add sugars and beat well for about 1-2 minutes
5. In go the eggs one by one, beat 30 seconds between additions then add the vanilla extract.
6. Gradually add the flour and beat until just combined.
7. Add the peanuts + chocolate/peanut butter chunks/chips and mix just enough to disperse, i.e. a few seconds.
8. Bake for 35-45 minutes, just until a toothpick comes out mostly clean.
9. Give it 5 minutes then remove the parchment/ foil from the pan and set the blondies aside on a rack to cool down
10. Cut into squares and serve', 335, 4.91, 32.63, 21.44, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/dorie-greenspans-peanuttiest-blondies/'),
('Oreo Cheesecake Jar', NULL, 'Kids or no kids- this Oreo Cheesecake in a jar is a fav at every party!', '24 Oreo Cookies
12 oz Cream Cheese
1/3 cup Whipping Cream
1/3-1/2 cup Icing Sugar (depending on your preference)
1 tsp Vanilla Extract
1/2 cup Chocolate Chips
1/3 cup Whipping Cream', '1. Crush Oreos in a food processor
2. Whip the cream cheese until soft and then add the icing sugar, whipped cream, and vanilla - mix on low until combined then turn up the speed and whip for another 1-2 minutes until fluffy
3. Fold/Stir in half the oreo crumbs - you can do a little less if you like, there''s no hard and fast rule here
4. Warm your cream until just simmering, pour it over your chocolate chips and stir until just smooth.
5. Note: I used 4 jars with a 2/3 cup capacity, how many you get will depend on the jar you use
6. Divide your oreo crumbs into four ''sections'' - i just separate them out on the plate I am using
7. From each section place half the Oreo crumbs on the bottom of each jar, add a layer of cheesecake filling (piping bag is easiest), the remaining crumbs, more cheesecake and top it with Ganache.
8. Refrigerate for 1-2 hours at least before serving, can be made a day ahead', 704, 8.43, 39.03, 58.35, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/oreo-cheesecake-jars-so-so-good/'),
('Turkey Sandwiches Three Ways', NULL, '[Serving count estimated at 12 (whole roast, gathering-size) -- source recipe didn''t list servings; verify before treating as exact.]', '2 Tortillas (large)
4 oz cream cheese
Sprinkling of your favourite spice mix - Cajun, Tandoori, Salt + Chili Powder + Cumin
1/4 cup minced cucumber
6-8 slices Smoked Turkey (or Plain)
3 tbsp mayo
2 tbsp buffalo hot sauce (if using other omit ketchup)
1 tsp ketchup
1/2 tsp cayenne
1/4 tsp garlic powder (optional)
salt and pepper
6 mini croissants
cheese slices
greens for croissant sandwich
6 slices deli turkey meat, cut in half for easier filling!
1/2 tomato
2 green chilies
1 cup roughly chopped cilantro
4-5 mint leaves (optional)
1 clove garlic
1/2 tsp cumin powder
salt
butter
8 slices of bread
8 slices of Turkey Deli meat', '1. Spread half the cream cheese on a tortilla
2. Sprinkle over half the cucumber and your favourite seasoning
3. Layer on half the turkey, roll up, and cut into spirals. Repeat for a second set of rolls.
4. Combine the first 6 ingredients for the sauce
5. Cut croissant across making sure not to separate it into two pieces and slather on some buffalo mayo on both ''sides''
6. Add the turkey, greens, and cheese. Repeat until your croissants are used up. Extra sauce can be served on the side or refrigerated for two weeks!
7. Blitz the first 7 ingredients, using a tiny splash of water to make it blendable.
8. Butter both sides of the bread, spread the chutney, add the turkey, cut into tiny sandwiches for prettier presentation', 164, 8.38, 13.63, 8.51, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/turkey-sandwiches-three-tasty-ways/'),
('Sun-dried Tomato & Chicken Pasta', NULL, NULL, '16 oz Pasta (one box - I used Penne)
3/4 lb Boneless Chicken cut into bite sized pieces
3/4 tsp salt
1/2 tsp pepper
1/2 tsp red chilli powder
1.5 tbsp olive oil
1/2 cup minced onion
5-6 cloves garlic
1 tsp red chilli flakes (or less)
1 cup chicken stock
1 1/2 cup cream
3/4 cup sun-dried tomatoes (jarred kind, drained of oil)
2 cups spinach (chopped)
1 cup mozzarella or monterey jack
2-3 tbsp Chopped Basil
Parmesan Cheese (grated)
Freshly Cracked Black Pepper', '1. Mix the chicken with the seasonings and olive oil and set aside. I usually do this on the chopping board I used for the chicken.
2. Bring a large pot of generously salted water to boil, then add the pasta and boil as per package directions. You can start the sauce while this happens
3. Reserve one cup of pasta water before draining
4. Heat a saute pan on medium high heat and add the chicken pieces in one even layer, cook for two minutes on each side and remove from the pan
5. Without wiping the pan add a little olive oil (if needed) and saute the onions, garlic, and red chilli flakes on medium heat until the onions are translucent.
6. Take care not to burn the garlic. Turn the heat down if it starts to darken too quickly.
7. Add the sun-dried tomatoes to the pan and cook for a minute.
8. For a smooth sauce remove most of the sauce ingredients from the pan and blitz them in a mini blender with one cup chicken stock
9. Pour the mix back into the pan, add the chicken and bring to a simmer
10. Turn the heat off and add one cup of the cream, the spinach, and the cheese
11. Mix with your cooked pasta and adjust the consistency with the remaining half cup cream and the pasta water
12. Now taste and adjust seasoning per taste.
13. Top with Basil and Parmesan and enjoy with warm garlic bread and a side salad.', 571, 31.62, 18.71, 41.7, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/sun-dried-tomato-chicken-pasta/'),
('Chanay ki Daal Instant Pot / Stovetop - Pakistani Recipe', NULL, 'A simple Pakistani daal recipe that requires a few ingredients for healthy every day comfort food. Instant Pot and Stove top timings for your convenience!', '1 cup chana daal (split chickpeas) ((soaked for a few hours, see notes for unsoaked))
2-4 cups water ((2 for IP, 4 for Stovetop))
1-2 tomato finely chopped or 1-2 tbsp of Passata
1 tsp salt
3/4 tsp red chilli powder
1/2 tsp coriander powder
1/4 tsp turmeric powder
1/4 cup chopped cilantro
lemon juice (according to taste)
2-3 green chillies, sliced or horizontally split
3 tbsp neutral oil
1/2 onion thinly sliced
3-4 whole dried red chillies
1/2 tsp cumin seeds', '1. Put the first seven ingredients into your instant pot and put on Manual, High Pressure for 10 minutes. Let the pressure naturally release, i.e. don''t do anything until it releases on it''s own (15-20 minutes). For unsoaked daal and stovetop timings are in the post.
2. The daal should be tender but holding shape, mash lightly to thicken
3. Put the IP on Saute, medium heat. Adjust thickness of daal according to preference - cook down to thicken, add water to thin.
4. Add the cilantro, green chillies, a little lemon juice and adjust seasoning (I usually add more salt)
5. Combine the first 7 ingredients in a pot and bring it them to a boil on medium high heat.
6. Simmer partially covered on low heat for 35-45 minutes or until it holds its shape but is cooked through. Adjust water if needed.
7. Once the daal is done, adjust thickness to liking by either drying out the daal or adding more water and then adjust seasoning and add in your cilantro, chilies, and lemon juice.
8. Heat a lug of oil in a small frying pan
9. When it shimmers add your sliced onions, whole red chillies and cumin seeds
10. Brown the onions and the pour the baghaar over the cooked daal. Eat with roti or rice.', 190, 8.94, 22.83, 8.78, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/chana-daal-instant-pot/'),
('Kalya/Murghi ka Salan or Pakistani Chicken Curry', NULL, 'A curry that gets its deep but light flavours from caramelized onions and mild spices', '1 Pound Chicken Breast Meat cut into 2 inch pieces
½ cup oil
1 large or 2 medium onions
1 tsp whole black peppercorns
1 tsp cumin seeds
1 heaped tbsp garlic or 5 minced cloves of garlic
1 tsp salt
½ tsp turmeric powder
1 ½ tsp coriander powder
½ to 1 tsp red chilli powder
1- 1 1/2 tsp salt
1/3 cup chopped cilantro
4-5 Whole green chillies (optional)
1/2 tsp garam masala powder', '1. Heat oil in a heavy bottomed pot
2. Add the cumin seeds and whole black pepper
3. When the cumin seeds start to sizzle then add the onions
4. Cook on medium heat stirring occasionally until the onions are mostly a rich brown
5. Now add the garlic paste, saute for a minute then add the red chili powder, turmeric, coriander powder and salt.
6. If at any time during the process the spices or onions start to burn add a splash of hot water.
7. Cook stirring frequently for about a minute then add the chicken pieces, stirring them at regular intervals until the look cooked/white from all sides.
8. Pour 1.5-2 cups of hot water into the pot, bring to a boil and then simmer covered for 30 minutes. The chicken should be nice and tender.
9. Increase the heat and dry up the masala, as you do so the onions will break down and form a beautiful cohesive paste. You can skip this step if you''re pressed for time and simply adjust the consistency of the curry to your liking.
10. Once the masalas become a paste and the oil rises to the top (bhunn) then add hot water as per your preference along with the green chilies and bring the mixture to a boil.
11. Turn the heat off, add the garam masala, adjust the seasoning, top with cilantro and serve.', 390, 27.13, 4.97, 30.71, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/murghi-ka-salan-chicken-curry-version-2/'),
('Kachay Qeemay ke Kabab or Galawat ke Kabab', NULL, 'A kabab with a creamy spiced interior studded with diced onions and chillies', '2 lb ground beef (lean)
1/2 - 3/4 cup papaya paste / ground papaya
1 1/4 cup besan, roasted
2 tbsp ginger paste
1 1/4 cup minced onion (2 medium)
8-10 roughly chopped green chilies
2-2.5 tsp salt ((for Pakistan use 2 as the salt is sharper))
1 tsp red chili powder/ cayenne
1 tsp red chili flakes
1 tsp pepper
1 tbsp garam masala powder
2 tsp cumin seeds, dry roasted and ground
1 tsp coriander seeds, dry roasted and ground', '1. Combine all the ingredients and leave it marinate for at least 6 hours or preferably over night
2. When ready to eat fry them in oil on medium low heat, frying at a high heat will make the kababs hard, you want to cook the inside and char the outside a little.
3. Serve hot with chapati', 522, 33.0, 22.72, 32.81, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/kachay-qeemay-kay-kabab-or-galawat-kay-kabab/'),
('Fish Karahi', NULL, 'A tomato rich classic Karahi made with flaky fish, this Fish Karahi with it''s rich easy flavor is such a weeknight fave!', '400 g Boneless white fish fillets
½ tsp turmeric powder
½ tsp salt
Juice of half a lemon
1 Sprig curry leaves
½ tsp kalonji/nigella seeds
1/2 tsp mustard seeds
¼ tsp fenugreek seeds
5-6 cloves crushed garlic – or 1 tbsp garlic paste
7-8 tomatoes (roma preferred)
1/2-3/4 tsp salt ((start with half))
1/2 tsp red chilli flakes
½ tsp chili powder
1 tbsp of butter (optional)
1 tbsp heaped kasuri methi i.e dried fenugreek leaves
Freshly cracked pepper
2-4 green chillies finely sliced
Handful of chopped cilantro
Juleinned ginger (optional)', '1. Cut your fish into fairly large chunks – mine were about 2*2 inches. Sprinkle them with the turmeric powder, salt, and juice of one lemon and set aside.
2. Warm oil in your pan on medium high heat and roughly chop your tomatoes.
3. When the oil is hot add the seeds i.e. fenugreek, and kalonji and curry leaves and just wait for them to splutter and become aromatic.
4. Now add your garlic, let it cook for 30 seconds and then add your tomatoes, salt, chili powder, and chili flakes.
5. Mix well and cook the tomatoes on high heat, stirring constantly until they get dark red and caramelly looking. This takes me about 10 minutes in a large wok.
6. If you are up for it then taste your spice mix, adjust seasoning if necessary, then place your fish pieces in the pan and cook for 3 minutes.
7. Carefully flip and let the fish cook through, another 2-4 minutes depending on the fish, a piece pressed will flake easily.
8. Drop the heat and add the butter, kasuri methi, fresh pepper, give it a gentle stir, adjust seasoning.
9. Garnish with cilantro, ginger, chilies and dig in!', 243, 26.86, 17.33, 8.23, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/fish-kadhaikarahi-or-fish-in-tomato-sauce/'),
('Strawberry Tart with No Roll Crust', NULL, NULL, '9 tbsp butter (room temp)
1/2 cup sugar
1 egg
1 egg yolk
1/4 tsp almond extract
1/2 tsp lemon extract (can use vanilla in place of these)
1 1/2 cup flour
1/2 cup cornmeal
1/2 tsp salt
2 tsp baking powder
coarse sugar for sprinkling (optional)
3/4 cup strawberries (use your softer ones here)
1/2 cup + 1 tbsp water
1/2 cup + 1 tbsp sugar
2 tbsp + 1 tsp cornstarch
2 tsp lemon juice
zest of one lemon
1/4 tsp salt
2 1/2 -3 cups sliced strawberries', '1. Whisk the flour, cornmeal, salt and baking powder in a bowl and set aside
2. Cream the butter and sugar
3. Add egg, egg yolk and extracts, mix to combine
4. Gradually add the dry ingredients to the wet just until the mixture comes together
5. Shape 2/3 of the dough into a disc, wrap in plastic wrap
6. Shape the remaining dough into a log, wrap in plastic wrap
7. Refrigerate for 3-4 hours or overnight
8. Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F
9. Remove the dough disc from the fridge, let it sit for 15 minutes then use the heel of your palm to flatten it and spread into a unbuttered tart pan, you can also break pieces and press down if that is easier
10. Once the dough is evenly spread then add the filling
11. Remove the dough log from the fridge, slice into slim rounds and arrange over the filling.
12. Sprinkle with coarse sugar and bake until the pastry is golden brown, i.e. for 20-25 minutes.
13. Mash the 3/4 cup strawberries, add into a small saucepan, bring to a boil and simmer for 3 minutes
14. Strain into a measuring cup and discard the pulp. Add just enough water to bring the liquid to 3/4 cup
15. Now add the sugar, cornstarch, lemon juice, zest and salt into the saucepan along with the strained juice, bring to a boil, stirring constantly
16. Cook till the mixture is thick and clear looking, 3 to 5 minutes
17. Remove from the heat, cool a little then add sliced strawberries, let mix cool to room temperature before adding to the crust', 381, 5.73, 54.84, 16.0, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/strawberry-tart/'),
('Better than Halal Guys Chicken and Rice', NULL, 'Inspired by the Halal Guys Chicken and Rice, this recipe turns the flavours up making it a crowd favorite!', '2 tablespoons lemon juice
1 tablespoon fresh oregano
1/2 teaspoon ground coriander
3 garlic cloves
1/4 cup light olive oil
Kosher salt and freshly ground black pepper
1 ½ pound chicken breast/boneless thigh diced into 1.5 inch cubes
Generous dollop yogurt – I used greek since I had it on hand (for the white sauce)
1 tablespoon vegetable or canola oil
2 tablespoons unsalted butter
1/2 teaspoon turmeric
1/2 teaspoon ground cumin
2 cups long-grain or Basmati rice
3 1/2 cups chicken broth (low sodium)
Kosher salt and freshly ground black pepper
10 oz. Greek yogurt
1/2 c. mayonnaise
1 Tbsp. white vinegar or red wine vinegar
1.5 Tbsp. lemon juice (½ lemon)
1 Tbsp. olive oil
3 garlic cloves (crushed)
1-2 tsp dill (dry or fresh)
1 tbsp cold water
Salt to taste
10-12 dried red chili peppers (or 2tbsp chilli flakes)
7 cloves garlic (minced)
3/4-1 teaspoon salt
4 tablespoons olive oil
2 teaspoon ground coriander
1.5 teaspoon caraway seeds
1 teaspoon cumin
1 tsp paprika powder
1 tbsp vinegar/lemon juice
Iceberg Lettuce cut into large chunks for serving', '1. Iceberg Lettuce cut into large chunks for serving
2. Combine all the ingredients – minus the chicken in a blender. Blend, taste, season, and marinade the chicken in this mix for 1-4 hours.
3. FIrst Method: On a grill pan or a grill, 2-3 minutes on each side, don''t overcook!
4. Second Method: Cook in a saucepan till tender. The when it''s time to eat spread it out on a lightly greased foil lined baking sheet, drizzle with a little oil and broil for 2-3 minutes to char.
5. Melt the butter over medium heat in a large Dutch oven.
6. Add the turmeric and cumin and cook until fragrant, but not browned, about 1 minute.
7. Add the rice and stir to coat. Cook, stirring frequently, until the rice is lightly toasted, about 4 minutes.
8. Add the chicken broth. Season to taste with salt and pepper. Raise the heat to high and bring to a boil. Cover, reduce to a simmer, and cook for 15 minutes.
9. After 15 minutes check on it, if the rice has not cooked through then add a splash of water and continue to let it cook tightly covered.
10. Whisk all the ingredients together. Taste, adjust seasoning.
11. Soak the dried chilies in hot water for 30 minutes. Drain and deseed. Use your kitchen shears to snip the chillies into a small food processor (I used my magic bullet) and blitz with the olive oil.
12. Then add the remaining ingredients and blend to form a smooth paste. Taste – adjust seasoning if necessary, mine was pretty spicy so I used it in moderation.
13. When you’re ready to eat then plate your rice, top with chicken, drizzle with white sauce, serve the hot sauce on the side or drizzle it across the top as well. Add some iceberg on the side and enjoy. Mmmmm…', 984, 58.7, 48.63, 60.38, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/halal-cart-style-chicken-and-rice-2/'),
('Kala Chana or Kalay Chanay', NULL, 'A black chickpea dish that is a Pakistani classic, perfect for iftar during Ramadan or really any time of the year :)', '2 cups black chickpeas or kalay chanay
1 onion, diced
3/4 tsp cumin seeds
1.5 tsp ginger paste
1.5 tsp garlic paste
2 tsp salt
2 tsp red chilli powder
1 tsp coriander powder
1/2 tsp turmeric
1-2 diced tomatoes (I prefer one)
2-3 tbsp tamarind pulp
1 tsp Garam Masala powder
Cilantro
Green Chillies', '1. Soak your black chickpeas overnight, rinse the water off.
2. Heat oil in your IP/Pressure Cooker. For IP Saute on Medium.
3. Saute cumin seeds till you can really smell them sizzling and then add the diced onions
4. Cook stirring occasionally till slightly golden then add the ginger and garlic pastes and saute for a minute
5. Then add the Salt, Red Chilli Powder, Coriander Powder, Turmeric, and stir fry for a minute
6. Add the diced tomato and saute until it''s cooked to a rich paste
7. Add the black chickpeas, stir to cook and then add 2 1/2 cups of hot water to your Instant Pot and set it on Manual for 25 minutes . Let it release naturally
8. Check the consistency, saute to reduce water or add water and bring to a boil according to your personal preference
9. Then add the tamarind pulp and garam masala, let simmer for 2-3 minutes then garnish with desired toppings.', 287, 14.73, 49.58, 4.59, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/kalay-chanay-in-an-instant-pot/'),
('Soft Dahi Baray', NULL, '[Serving count estimated at 16 (batch of individual pieces) -- source recipe didn''t list servings; verify before treating as exact.]', 'Yogurt 2 pounds or about 1 ½ times a 750g yogurt carton
1 tbsp sugar
2 tsp salt
1 ½ tsp red chilli powder
1 to 1 ½ tsp cumin powder
1 cup ma’ash/urad daal – the white kind covered with water and soaked overnight ((150g))
¼ teaspoon baking soda
½ teaspoon cumin powder
½ teaspoon red chilli powder
½ teaspoon salt
1/2 inch piece ginger (peeled, roughly chopped)
Chaat Masala Powder
Red Chilli Powder
Tamarind Chutney
Finely Chopped Cilantro
Coriander/Mint Chutney', '1. Combine the yogurt, sugar and spices along with ½ cup of water and whisk. I suggest starting with half the amount of chilli powder and cumin powder unless like me you are a fan.
2. Taste and check seasoning. Put it in the fridge while you work on the dumplings.
3. Drain the maash ki Daal making sure to reserve about 1/3 cup of soaking liquid.
4. Grind all the baray ingredients in a blender along with 1/4 cup of the daal water. Only add more if absolutely necessary. You want a very thick paste.
5. Transfer the mixture to a bowl
6. For softer Dahi Baray: Whisk energetically to create volume in the batter, about 4-5 minutes with a large whisk. 2 minutes with an electric mixer works.
7. Heat a skillet and add 2 inches of oil and put on medium-high heat for the oil to heat through.
8. Meanwhile get another pan or bowl – at least 10 inches in diameter and fill it 2/3 of the way with water. Add a pinch of salt in the water
9. Now get a tray or platter and line it with paper towels to help drain the grease from the dumplings.
10. Once the oil heats up then gently place a dollop of the batter into the hot oil.
11. After a minute and a half the dumpling will turn a lovely golden color at which point you should turn them over and cook for another minute and a half.
12. Remove from the oil and drain on paper towels.
13. Put the dumplings in the water bath for a few minutes
14. Pour a layer of yogurt mix into your dish of choice.
15. Remove the dumplings from the water one by one, gently squeezing them beneath your palms to drain the excess water and then lay them out in rows on top of the yogurt until your dish is filled.
16. Top with enough of the yogurt to adequately cover the dumplings and refrigerate.
17. Leave it for atleast an hour so the flavours soak through the dumplings.
18. Top with your garnishes of choice', 11, 0.32, 2.03, 0.33, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/dahi-baray-lentil-dumplings-in-a-spicy-tangy-yogurt/'),
('Easy Lemon Mousse', NULL, 'A simple lemon mousse that you can make ahead!', '1 cups whipping cream
300 ml condensed milk
1/3-1/2 cup lemon juice (1/2 if you want it tart!)
2 tsp gelatin (powdered) ((notes))
2 cups biscuit crumbs (recommend: ginger), for layering
a few drops of yellow food colour', '1. Gelatin: put 3 tbsp of water in a bowl, scatter the 2 tsp of gelatin over top. let it sit until it absorbs into the water (a few minutes) then heat it in the microwave for 30 seconds, if it doesn''t dissolve into a liquid then heat it some more. Set aside to cool
2. Whip the cream on medium high speed until peaks form
3. Mix in the condensed milk on medium speed, then the lemon juice, and finally the dissolved (cooled) gelatin. Taste to adjust for tartness (more lemon) or more sweetness (icing sugar). I like this as is
4. Layer the crumbs (if using) at the bottom of a dish then gently spoon the lemon mousse on top and smoothen it. Chill for a minimum of 2 hours and decorate as desired.', 211, 4.45, 15.39, 14.79, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/lemon-velvet-a-3-ingredient-wonder/'),
('Tehri - a Chatpata Version', NULL, 'This Tehri is a flavor filled version of the classic vegetarian yellow rice with potatoes', '2 cups basmati rice (washed and soaked)
1 1/2 to 2 cups potatoes sliced into 1/2 cm thick squares
1 onion diced
4 tomatoes finely diced
1-2 sprigs of curry leaves
1/2 tsp nigella/onion seeds/kalonji
1/2 tsp cumin seeds
2-3 finely sliced green chillies
2 tsp salt
1 tsp turmeric
1 1/2 tsp red chilli powder
1/2 tsp coriander powder
a glug of neutral oil - enough to cook the bottom of your pan
optional: lemon for squeezing, green chilies for garnish', '1. Take out a nice big pot, preferably non stick, but if you use a heavy bottomed one then increase the oil and make sure you keep checking for sticking (add a little water).
2. Heat the oil and add in your cumin seeds, nigella seeds, and curry leaves.
3. When it gets spluttery and aromatic add your onions and green chillies and saute on until the onion starts to brown at the edges.
4. Then add the rest of your spices and stir fry until they darken slightly, if they stick to the bottom of the pan add a splash of water.
5. Then add your tomatoes and cooked till the ''wetness'' sautes out and you''re life with a rich paste with the oil rising above it - in Urdu we call this Bhunna
6. Add your potatoes and saute for a minute or two.
7. Now add your rice, and then add just enough water that you have approximately half an inch of water rising above your rice. Now some brands cook quicker than others so please adjust the water accordingly. In a pinch you can add more, but taking water away – that’s not so doable.
8. Bring the water to a boil, and cook on medium till the water level drops to that off the rice, then simmer on low heat to tender fluffy perfection. Again if your brand of rice cooks quickly then please start with less water and watch your cooking times!
9. Top with a little lemon juice and sliced green chilies and serve hot with raita and kachumbar', 436, 9.77, 95.38, 1.43, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/tehri/'),
('EASY Pasanday Recipe - Instant Pot & Stove Top', NULL, 'thin fillets of beef/mutton, with a finger looking good masala!', '1 lb beef or mutton pasanday
1/3 cup neutral cooking oil
4-6 black peppers
2-3 whole cloves
1 inch cinnamon stick
1 black cardamom (bari illaichi)
1 onion, diced
3/4 inch piece of ginger - grated (or 1 rounded tsp of ginger paste)
6 cloves crushed/minced garlic (or 1 rounded tsp garlic paste)
1/2-3/4 tsp salt
3/4 tsp coriander powder
1/2 tsp red chili flakes
1/2 tsp red chili powder (cayenne)
1/4 tsp turmeric powder
1 tsp garam masala
1/2 cup yogurt, whipped, room temperature', '1. Heat the oil in your Instant Pot on Saute, Normal heat.
2. When it shimmers add the cinnamon, cloves, whole black pepper, and cardamom, saute for 30 seconds and when aromatic add the onions
3. Saute the onions stirring occasionally until the edges turn golden brown
4. Then add your ginger and garlic, saute for a minute
5. Now add the meat followed by the spices (salt, chili powder, chili flakes, garam masala, coriander powder, turmeric)
6. Saute stirring frequently until all the meat changes color
7. Now add a cup and a half of hot water, stir and set the instant pot on manual for 8 minutes OR add 2 cups of hot water and simmer on low for 30.
8. Quick release when done and check for tenderness, if your meat isn''t as soft as you would like you can simmer it for a little longer otherwise turn on the saute mode to dry up the masala. For stove top, do the same.
9. When the oil rises to the top then turn the Instant Pot or stove off and gradually add your yogurt
10. The yogurt will cook in the residual heat, stir gently to combine, taste, adjust seasoning and serve.', 536, 23.01, 17.74, 42.78, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/easy-instant-pot-pasanday-recipe/'),
('Nihari', NULL, '[Serving count estimated at 6 (main course, family-size) -- source recipe didn''t list servings; verify before treating as exact.]', '2 lb Large chunks of beef/veal - 3 inch pieces
1-2 lb bones
2 tbsp salt
1 1/2 tbsp ginger paste
1 1/2 tbsp garlic paste
1 tbsp red chilli powder
1 tbsp kashmiri chilli powder
1 tbsp coriander powder
1/2 tsp turmeric powder
Ghee/Oil for cooking
1 large onion
1.5 tbsp coriander seeds
1.5 tbsp saunf
1.5 tsp whole black pepper
1.5 tsp whole cloves
1/2 tbsp cumin seeds
1 bay leaf
1/2 tsp grated nutmeg
2 1-inch cinnamon sticks
2-3 piece mace
3 black cardamoms
4-6 green cardamoms
1 piece dried ginger (small, can sub with 1/2 tbsp of gingepowder)
6 whole red chillies (round)
1 tsp kalonji
2 pieces of peepli or 3-4 kabab chini (optional)
lemon wedges
sliced green chillies
julienned ginger', '1. Dry roast all the ingredients in a frying pan (no oil), grind to a powder. Set aside
2. Heat oil in a large pot
3. Thinly slice your onion, fry till golden brown then spread on paper towels to dry. (we will use these at the end)
4. Add all the remaining ingredients in the first list and stir fry the meat until its browned and the masala is cooked - about 4-5 minutes
5. Then add your Nihari Masala Mix and 7 cups of water and stir well.
6. Pressure cook for 45-50 minutes or slow cook for 4-5 hours undisturbed to get beautifully tender meat. For slow cooking stove top, bring the mixture to a boil then let it simmer covered.
7. Once the time is up skim any greyish scum that may rise to the top and discard.
8. Crush the onions and mix in, bring the nihari to a boil
9. If you are serving this another time then set it aside for the nihari to cool.
10. When ready to eat then dissolve 1/3 cup atta in 1 cup water and whisk briskly as you add it to the nihari
11. The nihari will thicken as it cooks - 10 to 15 minutes
12. Adjust consistency per liking (more water or atta+water), just remember you need to simmer after adding it to lose the raw taste.
13. Heat a few tbsp of oil in a small saucepan and add 1.5 tbsp of kashmiri laal mirch (for colour) and add it on top of the nihari like a tadka/baghaar.', 763, 58.99, 18.91, 50.58, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/nihari/'),
('No Oil Lemon Pickle - Khattay Leemoo', NULL, '[Serving count estimated at 20 (condiment, tbsp-size servings) -- source recipe didn''t list servings; verify before treating as exact.]', '4 Organic lemons, washed and scrubbed
2 1/4 tbsp Pickling Salt
Optional add ins: green chillies, nigella seeds, cumin seeds, peppercorns, star anise, etc.', '1. Halved your scrubbed lemons and juice them most of the way. Save the juice for another use
2. Cut each half into six pieces or slim slivers
3. Layer the lemon pieces into the bottom of the jar, press them down enough to create an approximate 1.5-2 inch layer
4. Add your add ins of choice (or none at all) and sprinkle with 3/4 tbsp pickling salt
5. Repeat until the jar is filled to the top
6. Shut the lid tightly and leave in the sun for 10 days. The lemon rind will change colour, the salt will leach some liquid out of the lemon, this is all normal (and good!).
7. Invert the jars every day to distribute the natural pickling liquid. Check on it after 10 days, the rind should be nice and soft, if not then leave out for another few days
8. Eat with daal chawal, khichri, biryani, matar pulao.', 3, 0.13, 1.09, 0.03, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/no-oil-lemon-pickle-khattay-leemoo/'),
('Chanay ki Daal ka Halwa', NULL, 'a decadent classic halwa that is irresistible in the winter months!', '1 cup chana daal (soaked overnight)
1 litre whole milk
1 1/4 cup ghee (or butter, or combination)
3-4 whole cloves
3-4 whole cardamoms, slightly smashed
1/2 tsp cardamom powder
small pinch Saffron (optional)
1 1/2 cup sugar
1/8 tsp salt', '1. SImmer the chanay ki daal in the milk until tender, this can take an hour to 90 minutes. When you press the daal it should break very easily.
2. Cook down the milk on low flame (milk boils over fast) so it is an inch above the chanay ki daal
3. Let cool then puree. If the chana daal does not have any liquid left in it it will not puree since it is naturally thick .
4. Heat ghee in a non stick wok on medium heat and add cloves and cardamom
5. When they start to sputter add your chana daal puree.
6. Stir vigorously, first you will see the ghee absorb into the daal, but the mixture will still be beige in color
7. Add the cardamom powder, salt, and saffron into the halwa, keep stirring
8. When the halwa gets to a caramelly color, about 15-20 minutes then add the sugar. Make sure you to stir the halwa contiuously. If the halwa feels like it''s catching/burning then turn the heat down.
9. Once the sugar goes in it will thicken the halwa, but as it cooks the halwa will become more liquid-y. Keep cooking (and stirring) till it reaches the a rich caramel.
10. If the mixture looks thick or chewy then add a splash of milk to loosen it then press into a plate.
11. Scatter blanched sliced almonds over top and cut into pieces.
12. You can also freeze the halwa for upto 3 months!', 794, 10.77, 74.66, 52.38, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/chanay-ki-daal-ka-halwa/'),
('Behari Chicken', NULL, 'Chicken marinated in behari boti spices and cooked to perfection', '1 large chicken cut into 2 leg pieces and 2 breast pieces (tikka cuts (with skin removed))
1 large onion fried golden brown
1/2 cup yogurt
2 tsp salt or to taste
2 tsp roasted grounded cumin seeds (zeera)
2 tsp red chili powder
1 tsp crushed black pepper
1 tbsp garlic ginger paste
1 tsp garam masala powder
1 tsp of roasted poppy seeds (optional)
Oil for coating', '1. Wash and pat your chicken dry. Add cuts along the lengths of your chicken pieces.
2. In a blender add brown fried onions, along with yogurt and all the other spices. Blend until you get fine smooth paste.
3. Marinate the chicken pieces in the heavy marinade. Making sure you get all the nooks and crannies.
4. Cover the chicken and let it marinade for 4 hours or overnight. You can smoke your chicken with a coal at this point.
5. Remove the chicken from the fridge at least 30 mins before you have to make it.
6. Cooking methods:
7. a. On a BBQ grill. - This is pretty straight forward. You fire up a grill and grill on both sides till its nice and charred
8. b. Pan frying. - Pan fry the pieces on a pan at high flame on both sides for about 4 mins on each side or till you get a nice color on both sides. Then reduce the flame to low. Cover the pan and let it cook for another 10 mins.
9. c. Baking - Grease a pan with oil or butter and place your chicken pieces on it. Coat the chicken with oil as well. Cover the chicken in foil and Bake in a preheated oven at 180 C for 375F or 15 mins. Remove the foil and Turn on the broil and bake for another 5 mins until you get a nice color on top. Take the chicken out, flip the pieces over and broil for another 5 mins.
10. Serve with some extra lemon slices to squeeze on top, onion slices and mint chutney.', 71, 3.31, 8.27, 3.36, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/pakistani-behari-chicken/'),
('Hanifia Sauce (Copycat Recipe)', NULL, 'Perfect for beef sliders, burgers, and especially hunter beef!', '1 1/2 cup water
2 tbsp oil
1 1/2 - 2 tbsp vinegar
1 tbsp red chili powder
1 tbsp mustard powder
1 tbsp salt
1-2 tbsp flour', '1. Combine all the ingredients in a small pot, whisk well to break up lumps
2. Bring to a boil, simmer till a thicker consistency - 5-10 minutes
3. Cool then drizzle over your your pulled beef (or hunter beef) and serve.', 63, 2.01, 4.32, 4.96, 'N', NULL, NULL, 'Flour & Spice — https://www.flourandspiceblog.com/hanifia-sauce-and-how-to-make-sliders/'),
('Soft Dahi Baray', NULL, '[Serving count estimated at 16 (batch of individual pieces) -- source recipe didn''t list servings; verify before treating as exact.]', 'Yogurt 2 pounds or about 1 ½ times a 750g yogurt carton
